/* Lecture 8 video lecture data: chapters, slide start times, timed bilingual transcript (generated). */
window.LEC = {"num":8,"videoBase":"https://wabyking.github.io/nlp2026-videos-2/lecture08/","parts":[{"n":1,"title":"The Final Project: Deliverables, Deadlines and Grading","blurb":"What you hand in and when: teams of up to three, a poster session on December 18, a six-page paper on December 25, and how the 55 percent is split.","file":"lecture08_part1.mp4","poster":"lecture08_part1.jpg","duration":700.6,"first":1,"last":14,"slides":[{"n":1,"title":"Title: Lecture 8","t":0.8},{"n":2,"title":"Contents","t":54.71},{"n":3,"title":"Part1. Introduction to the Final Project","t":103.17},{"n":4,"title":"Introduction","t":122.01},{"n":5,"title":"Introduction","t":174.72},{"n":6,"title":"Introduction","t":248.39},{"n":7,"title":"Introduction","t":309.49},{"n":8,"title":"Example of posters","t":353.46},{"n":9,"title":"HuatuoGPT, trained on ChatGPT and real-world data, creates doctor-like, accessible responses. Its conversational ability","t":399.14},{"n":10,"title":"Introduction","t":453.0},{"n":11,"title":"Introduction","t":496.43},{"n":12,"title":"Introduction","t":530.34},{"n":13,"title":"Introduction","t":582.25},{"n":14,"title":"Introduction","t":636.71}],"sents":[[0.8,2.98,1,"Hi everyone, welcome back.","大家好，欢迎回来。"],[3.33,9.28,1,"Last time we built LLM agents: a model in a loop with tools, memory and feedback.","上一讲我们构建了大模型智能体：一个在循环中使用工具、记忆和反馈的模型。"],[9.63,14.82,1,"And we saw that the harness around the model often matters as much as the model itself.","我们还看到，模型外面那层 harness，往往和模型本身一样重要。"],[15.17,16.78,1,"Today is a bit different.","今天有点不一样。"],[17.13,20.81,1,"There's no new architecture and no new training algorithm.","今天没有新的架构，也没有新的训练算法。"],[21.16,27.17,1,"Today is about you, and about the biggest single piece of work in this course: your final project.","今天讲的是你们，以及这门课里分量最重的一项工作：期末项目。"],[27.52,29.85,1,"It's fifty-five percent of your grade.","它占你总成绩的 55%。"],[30.2,38.51,1,"But more importantly, it's your chance to do a small piece of real research, where you ask your own question and find out the answer yourself.","但更重要的是，这是你做一项小小的真实研究的机会：提出你自己的问题，并亲自找到答案。"],[38.86,43.92,1,"I'll cover the rules and the grading, then spend most of the time on what you could work on.","我会先讲规则和评分，然后用大部分时间讲你们可以做什么。"],[44.27,51.85,1,"Then I'll show you some strong projects from past terms, and finish with the writing advice I give my own PhD students.","接着展示往届的一些优秀项目，最后分享我给自己博士生的写作建议。"],[52.2,53.31,1,"Let's get started.","我们开始吧。"],[54.56,57.73,2,"Here's the roadmap for today, in four parts.","这是今天的路线图，分四个部分。"],[58.08,65.12,2,"First, the basics of the final project: what you deliver, team rules, deadlines and how we grade.","第一，期末项目的基本要求：交什么、组队规则、截止日期，以及如何评分。"],[65.47,69.07,2,"Second, topic selection, which is the longest part.","第二，选题，这是篇幅最长的一部分。"],[69.42,78.42,2,"We'll go through the eight project tracks on the course website, some fresh ideas for brainstorming, and advice on how to pick a topic and who to talk to.","我们会过一遍课程网站上的八个项目方向、一些用于头脑风暴的新点子，以及如何选题、该找谁聊的建议。"],[78.77,84.0,2,"Third, outstanding projects from previous terms, so you can see what good looks like.","第三，往届的优秀项目，让你们看看好项目长什么样。"],[84.35,93.2,2,"And finally, I'll share what we've learned from past final projects about writing, because a good result written badly loses a lot of points.","最后，我会分享从往届项目中总结的写作经验，因为好的结果如果写得很糟，会丢很多分。"],[93.55,101.77,2,"The logic is simple: rules first, then what to work on, then what success looks like, then how to present it.","逻辑很简单：先讲规则，再讲做什么，然后看成功是什么样子，最后讲如何呈现。"],[103.02,104.66,3,"Let's start with the basics.","我们从基础开始。"],[105.01,113.44,3,"Before you pick a topic, you need to know exactly what you're delivering, who you can work with, when things are due, and how the points are split.","在选题之前，你需要清楚地知道要交什么、可以和谁合作、什么时候截止，以及分数怎么分配。"],[113.79,120.61,3,"None of it is complicated, but missing one deadline can cost you real marks, so please pay attention to the dates.","这些都不复杂，但错过一个截止日期就可能实打实地丢分，所以请留意这些日期。"],[121.86,131.48,4,"By now you've been through a lot with us: word vectors, language models, Transformers, LLMs, RL post-training and agents.","到现在，你们已经跟着我们学了很多：词向量、语言模型、Transformer、大模型、强化学习后训练，还有智能体。"],[131.83,137.2,4,"The final project is where you stop following our assignments and start asking your own question.","期末项目，就是你不再跟着我们的作业走，而开始提出自己问题的地方。"],[137.55,139.72,4,"The key word on this slide is excites.","这页幻灯片的关键词是“让你兴奋”。"],[140.07,145.43,4,"Pick a task or problem you actually care about, because you'll be living with it for about four weeks.","选一个你真正关心的任务或问题，因为接下来大约四周你都要和它朝夕相处。"],[145.78,149.1,4,"And that's much easier when you're curious about the answer.","如果你对答案真心好奇，这件事就会容易得多。"],[149.45,152.66,4,"Think of it as your first mini research project.","把它当作你的第一个迷你研究项目。"],[153.01,159.93,4,"You have a question, you build something or run something to answer it, you collect evidence, and then you communicate it.","你有一个问题，你搭建或运行一些东西来回答它，收集证据，然后把它讲出来。"],[160.28,165.02,4,"You communicate it twice: once as a paper, and once as a poster.","你要讲两次：一次写成论文，一次做成海报。"],[165.37,173.32,4,"That full cycle, from question to evidence to communication, is exactly what researchers and good engineers do every day.","从问题到证据再到表达，这个完整的循环，正是研究者和优秀工程师每天在做的事。"],[174.57,176.19,5,"Now, teams.","下面说组队。"],[176.54,182.38,5,"You can work alone or in a team, and the suggested team size is two or three.","你可以单独完成，也可以组队，建议的队伍规模是两到三人。"],[182.73,189.64,5,"A larger team is possible only if you explain how the workload and each person's responsibilities justify it.","更大的队伍也可以，但必须说明工作量和每个人的职责为什么需要这么多人。"],[189.99,196.64,5,"We actually recommend a team: you can split the work, review each other's code, and it's simply more fun.","我们其实推荐组队：可以分工，可以互相审查代码，而且就是更有意思。"],[196.99,199.87,5,"But the expectation scales with team size.","但期望会随着队伍规模而提高。"],[200.22,206.59,5,"A three-person team should take on something more ambitious than a solo project, and we'll judge it that way.","三人队应该挑战比单人项目更有野心的题目，我们也会按这个标准来评判。"],[206.94,211.82,5,"Your report has to include a contribution statement saying who did what.","你们的报告必须包含一份贡献声明，写明谁做了什么。"],[212.17,219.89,5,"Please make it concrete: A built the data pipeline, B ran the baselines, C wrote the analysis.","请写得具体：A 搭建了数据流水线，B 跑了基线，C 写了分析。"],[220.24,223.33,5,"Not just: everyone contributed equally.","而不是一句：大家贡献相同。"],[223.68,231.32,5,"You can also collaborate with people outside the course, maybe a senior in your lab or a friend at another university.","你也可以和课程以外的人合作，比如实验室的师兄师姐，或者其他大学的朋友。"],[231.67,235.93,5,"That's fine, as long as you clearly say which parts are your own work.","这没问题，只要你清楚说明哪些部分是你自己的工作。"],[236.28,242.29,5,"Team formation, together with the optional one-page proposal, is due on November thirteenth.","组队和可选的一页开题提案，截止日期都是 11 月 13 日。"],[242.64,246.99,5,"So if you haven't found teammates yet, now is the time to do it.","所以如果你还没找到队友，现在就是时候了。"],[248.24,252.29,6,"Two deliverables, two dates. Please put them in your calendar right now.","两项提交物，两个日期。请现在就把它们记进日历。"],[252.64,259.17,6,"The poster presentation is on December eighteenth, on site, using the poster template linked here.","海报展示在 12 月 18 日现场进行，请使用这里链接的海报模板。"],[259.52,266.39,6,"If you submit your poster file by five in the afternoon on December seventeenth, the teaching team prints it for you for free.","如果你在 12 月 17 日下午 5 点前提交海报文件，教学团队会免费帮你打印。"],[266.74,272.91,6,"Miss that deadline and you'll have to print it yourself and bring it along, so don't miss it.","错过这个截止时间，你就得自己打印再带过来，所以千万别错过。"],[273.26,279.03,6,"The final paper is due on December twenty-fifth, at eleven fifty-nine at night, as a PDF.","期末论文的截止时间是 12 月 25 日晚上 11 点 59 分，提交 PDF。"],[279.38,284.15,6,"Use the Overleaf template: just copy the project and edit your own version.","请使用 Overleaf 模板：复制这个项目，然后编辑你自己的版本。"],[284.5,288.21,6,"The limit is six pages of main text, not counting references.","篇幅上限是六页正文，不含参考文献。"],[288.56,295.61,6,"Treat that as a firm limit: extra pages won't earn you any extra points, so learn to cut.","请把它当作硬性上限：多写的页数不会给你带来任何加分，所以要学会删减。"],[295.96,300.08,6,"One practical consequence: the poster comes a week before the paper.","一个实际的后果是：海报比论文早一周。"],[300.43,304.25,6,"That means your main results need to be ready by mid-December.","这意味着你的主要结果要在 12 月中旬就准备好。"],[304.6,308.09,6,"So plan backwards from that date, not from Christmas.","所以请从那个日期往回倒推计划，而不是从圣诞节倒推。"],[309.34,312.07,7,"Here you can see the two parts side by side.","这里你可以并排看到这两个部分。"],[312.42,316.6,7,"On the left is a poster from a past team, StockGPT.","左边是往届一支队伍的海报，StockGPT。"],[316.95,320.68,7,"On the right is the first page of a past project report.","右边是往届一份项目报告的第一页。"],[321.03,325.32,7,"It's the same kind of project in two formats, for two different audiences.","同一类项目，两种形式，面向两类不同的读者。"],[325.67,329.63,7,"The poster is for someone walking past who gives you thirty seconds.","海报是给路过的人看的，他们只会给你三十秒。"],[329.98,334.76,7,"So it has to be visual, with a big method figure and a clear result chart.","所以它必须直观，有一张大的方法图和一张清楚的结果图。"],[335.11,343.56,7,"The paper is for a careful reader who wants the full argument: motivation, related work, method, experiments and analysis.","论文是给认真的读者看的，他们想看完整的论证：动机、相关工作、方法、实验和分析。"],[343.91,346.6,7,"So don't just paste your paper onto the poster.","所以，不要把论文直接贴到海报上。"],[346.95,352.06,7,"Think about what a stranger needs to see in thirty seconds to get curious about your work.","想一想：一个陌生人需要在三十秒内看到什么，才会对你的工作产生好奇。"],[353.31,355.5,8,"A couple more poster examples.","再看几张海报的例子。"],[355.85,360.46,8,"On the left is a collaborative search system with an interactive engine.","左边是一个带交互引擎的协同搜索系统。"],[360.81,366.45,8,"On the right is a quantum-inspired complex embedding poster from my own PhD years.","右边是我自己读博期间做的量子启发复数嵌入的海报。"],[366.8,369.08,8,"Look at the structure rather than the content.","请看结构，而不是内容。"],[369.43,378.54,8,"Both have a short introduction and motivation, then a framework or method figure that takes up a lot of space, then experiments and results.","两张海报都有简短的引言和动机，然后是占据大片空间的框架图或方法图，再是实验和结果。"],[378.89,382.28,8,"Text is in short blocks, not long paragraphs.","文字是一小块一小块的，而不是长段落。"],[382.63,387.17,8,"Your eye can travel from top left to bottom right and pick up the story.","你的视线可以从左上走到右下，顺着把故事读下来。"],[387.52,393.41,8,"That's the target: someone should understand your question and your main finding without you standing there.","这就是目标：即使你不在旁边，别人也能看懂你的问题和主要发现。"],[393.76,397.74,8,"And when you are standing there, the poster should support what you say.","而当你站在旁边时，海报应该为你的讲解提供支撑。"],[398.99,406.84,9,"This is the poster template we provide, filled in with HuatuoGPT, a medical LLM from our lab, as an example.","这是我们提供的海报模板，用我们实验室的医疗大模型 HuatuoGPT 填充作为示例。"],[407.19,412.14,9,"The header still mentions an older LLM course, but the layout is what matters.","页眉上还写着以前的一门大模型课程，但重要的是版式。"],[412.49,417.73,9,"Notice the blocks: title, authors, student IDs and email at the top.","注意这些区块：最上面是标题、作者、学号和邮箱。"],[418.08,423.73,9,"Then come the introduction, motivation, methodology and results blocks.","接下来是引言、动机、方法和结果几个区块。"],[424.08,427.92,9,"You can rearrange or rename the blocks as you like.","这些区块你可以随意调整顺序或重新命名。"],[428.27,435.15,9,"Look at how the methodology block is mostly one diagram, showing the data sources and the two training stages.","看方法这一块，主要就是一张图，展示了数据来源和两个训练阶段。"],[435.5,440.44,9,"And the results block is mostly charts comparing against other models.","而结果这一块，主要是和其他模型对比的图表。"],[440.79,445.52,9,"Also notice the QR codes at the bottom, for the demo and the GitHub repo.","还要注意底部的二维码，分别指向演示和 GitHub 仓库。"],[445.87,451.6,9,"That's a small touch, but at a busy poster session it lets people try your system later.","这是个小细节，但在熙熙攘攘的海报展上，它能让大家事后去试用你的系统。"],[452.85,459.43,10,"On the day itself, you'll stand by your poster and give a four-minute introduction of your project.","展示当天，你会站在海报旁，用四分钟介绍你的项目。"],[459.78,463.32,10,"Four minutes is short, much shorter than it feels.","四分钟很短，比你感觉的要短得多。"],[463.67,466.76,10,"My advice: rehearse with a timer.","我的建议是：掐着表排练。"],[467.11,469.47,10,"A good four-minute pitch has four parts.","一段好的四分钟讲解有四个部分。"],[469.82,477.71,10,"The question you asked, the one comparison figure that answers it, one failure case, and one honest limitation.","你提出的问题、回答这个问题的那张对比图、一个失败案例，以及一个坦诚的局限。"],[478.06,484.31,10,"If you have a demo, have it ready on a laptop, already loaded, not waiting for a server to start.","如果有演示，请在笔记本上提前准备好、加载好，而不是现场等服务器启动。"],[484.66,489.87,10,"Also, you'll be judging other groups too, so walk around, ask questions, and enjoy it.","另外，你们也要给其他组打分，所以多走走、多提问，好好享受。"],[490.22,495.03,10,"A poster session is one of the best parts of academic life.","海报展是学术生活中最美好的部分之一。"],[496.28,502.08,11,"For the final paper, you'll write it up and submit it through the BB system, which is Blackboard.","期末论文写好后，通过 BB 系统，也就是 Blackboard 提交。"],[502.43,508.19,11,"We give you a LaTeX template on Overleaf, linked right here, so you don't have to fight with formatting.","我们在 Overleaf 上提供了 LaTeX 模板，链接就在这里，省得你和排版较劲。"],[508.54,513.19,11,"My practical tip: don't wait until your experiments are finished to start writing.","我的实用建议是：不要等实验全部做完才开始写。"],[513.54,518.07,11,"Write a draft of the introduction and the related work in the first two weeks.","在头两周就写出引言和相关工作的初稿。"],[518.42,522.17,11,"Writing early forces you to say clearly what your question is.","早点写，会逼着你把自己的问题说清楚。"],[522.52,528.94,11,"And very often, you'll discover your plan has a gap while it's still cheap to fix.","而且你经常会发现计划里有漏洞，而这时候修补的代价还很小。"],[530.19,531.45,12,"Now the grading.","下面讲评分。"],[531.8,537.38,12,"The final project is fifty-five percent of your total grade, more than half of the course.","期末项目占总成绩的 55%，超过整门课的一半。"],[537.73,543.32,12,"It's split into the presentation at ten percent, and the report at forty-five percent.","它分为展示 10% 和报告 45% 两部分。"],[543.67,548.8,12,"The presentation score comes from ratings by other groups and the TAs, averaged.","展示分来自其他组和助教的打分，取平均值。"],[549.15,550.47,12,"Look at how it's split.","看看它是怎么分配的。"],[550.82,559.76,12,"Poster quality is only one percent, the oral presentation is four percent, and an overall subjective assessment is five percent.","海报质量只占 1%，口头讲解占 4%，整体主观评价占 5%。"],[560.11,562.61,12,"So a beautiful poster alone won't save you.","所以光有一张漂亮的海报救不了你。"],[562.96,567.91,12,"What matters is whether you can explain your work clearly, and with some energy.","关键在于你能否把工作讲清楚，而且讲得有激情。"],[568.26,575.29,12,"Yes, the five percent is subjective, and that's honest: it's how real conferences and real job interviews work too.","没错，这 5% 是主观的，我们坦白承认：真实的学术会议和求职面试也是这样。"],[575.64,580.85,12,"People remember whether your work was interesting, and whether you clearly understood it.","人们会记住你的工作是否有趣，以及你是否真正理解了它。"],[582.1,586.61,13,"The report is where most of the points are: forty-five percent.","报告是分数的大头：45%。"],[586.96,591.54,13,"Technical excitement is ten percent: is this interesting or useful?","技术吸引力占 10%：它有趣或有用吗？"],[591.89,596.38,13,"Technical soundness is fifteen percent, and the slide spells out what that means.","技术严谨性占 15%，幻灯片上写明了具体含义。"],[596.73,604.36,13,"A motivation, related work, a clear method, and an evaluation protocol with both numbers and examples.","要有动机、相关工作、清晰的方法，以及既有数字又有例子的评测方案。"],[604.71,609.42,13,"And an analysis of when and why your system works or fails.","还要分析你的系统在什么时候、为什么成功或失败。"],[609.77,613.5,13,"That last part is where many teams lose points.","最后这一点，正是很多队伍丢分的地方。"],[613.85,619.4,13,"A table of numbers is not an analysis; telling me why the numbers look the way they do is.","一张数字表格不是分析；告诉我这些数字为什么会是这样，才是分析。"],[619.75,625.36,13,"Notice that clarity of writing is also fifteen percent, exactly as much as soundness.","注意，写作清晰度同样占 15%，和严谨性完全一样多。"],[625.71,630.49,13,"That's deliberate, and it's why the last part of today is about writing.","这是有意为之，也是为什么今天最后一部分专门讲写作。"],[630.84,635.31,13,"Finally, five percent is individual contribution, evaluated per person.","最后，5% 是个人贡献，按每个人单独评定。"],[636.56,639.45,14,"And there are a few bonuses and one penalty.","此外还有几项加分和一项扣分。"],[639.8,643.87,14,"If a TA picks your project as their favourite, that's two percent.","如果某位助教把你的项目选为最爱，加 2%。"],[644.22,649.17,14,"Each TA nominates at most one project, and you can only earn this bonus once.","每位助教最多提名一个项目，而且这项加分只能拿一次。"],[649.52,656.21,14,"The instructor's favourite is one percent; I can nominate up to three projects, and you can earn both.","讲师最爱加 1%；我最多可以提名三个项目，而且两项加分可以同时获得。"],[656.56,662.96,14,"There's also an early-bird bonus of two percent, if you submit your report by the early deadline.","还有 2% 的早鸟加分，只要你在提前截止日期前提交报告。"],[663.31,667.82,14,"And there's one percent if the TAs can easily reproduce your results.","如果助教能轻松复现你的结果，再加 1%。"],[668.17,673.83,14,"So put clean code in your repo, with a README and the exact commands.","所以请在仓库里放上干净的代码，附上 README 和确切的运行命令。"],[674.18,679.11,14,"The penalty: a serious ethics concern costs one percent.","扣分项：严重的伦理问题扣 1%。"],[679.46,685.67,14,"Think about user data, consent, scraping, and human studies before you start, not after.","关于用户数据、知情同意、网页爬取和涉及人的研究，请在开始之前就考虑，而不是事后。"],[686.02,692.55,14,"And note that, bonuses included, the project credit is capped at fifty-five percent.","另外注意，包括加分在内，项目总分的上限是 55%。"],[692.9,698.76,14,"That's the logistics. Now for the more interesting question: what should you actually build?","以上是事务性安排。接下来是更有意思的问题：你到底该做什么？"]]},{"n":2,"title":"Choosing a Track: Agents and Training Your Own Model","blurb":"Two ways to pick a topic, the eight tracks and the project page's six rules, then Track A on agent harnesses and Track B on training your own model.","file":"lecture08_part2.mp4","poster":"lecture08_part2.jpg","duration":737.6,"first":15,"last":28,"slides":[{"n":15,"title":"Part2. Topic Selection","t":0.8},{"n":16,"title":"Topic Selection","t":23.89},{"n":17,"title":"Eight tracks for Fall 2026","t":76.65},{"n":18,"title":"How to use the project page","t":134.58},{"n":19,"title":"Track A: Agents & harness: tools, skills & iterative repair","t":205.88},{"n":20,"title":"Agent workflow","t":276.06},{"n":21,"title":"A New Skill","t":325.09},{"n":22,"title":"Automatic Survey","t":373.34},{"n":23,"title":"Track B: Train your own model: vertical models, new modalities & nanoGPT","t":429.75},{"n":24,"title":"Examples","t":490.77},{"n":25,"title":"Examples","t":549.75},{"n":26,"title":"Arabic LLMs","t":602.03},{"n":27,"title":"Speech LLMs","t":655.77},{"n":28,"title":"Special Support","t":708.94}],"sents":[[0.8,4.48,15,"So you know what to deliver and how it's graded.","现在你知道要交什么、怎么评分了。"],[4.83,7.23,15,"The harder question is what to work on.","更难的问题是：做什么。"],[7.58,17.08,15,"This part answers that: the eight tracks on our project page, some examples from our lab and past students, and new ideas to brainstorm with.","这一部分就来回答它：项目页面上的八个方向、我们实验室和往届同学的一些例子，以及一些头脑风暴的新点子。"],[17.43,22.49,15,"And some advice on choosing a topic you'll still care about in four weeks.","还有一些建议，帮你选一个四周后依然在乎的题目。"],[23.74,25.26,16,"You have two options.","你有两个选择。"],[25.61,29.39,16,"Option one: choose one of the briefs on the project page.","选择一：从项目页面上选一个课题简介。"],[29.74,33.8,16,"There are eight tracks, A to H, with seventy-seven briefs in total.","一共八个方向，从 A 到 H，总共 77 个课题简介。"],[34.15,37.62,16,"Each brief is basically a ready-made research plan.","每个简介基本上就是一份现成的研究计划。"],[37.97,42.54,16,"That's a great choice if you want a well-scoped project with a clear evaluation.","如果你想要一个范围明确、评测清楚的项目，这是很好的选择。"],[42.89,45.51,16,"Option two: propose your own topic.","选择二：自己提出题目。"],[45.86,50.59,16,"That's very welcome, with one condition: it has to be related to LLMs.","我们非常欢迎，只有一个条件：必须和大模型相关。"],[50.94,56.78,16,"If you already do research in a lab, or you have an idea you've been itching to try, go for it.","如果你已经在实验室做研究，或者有一个跃跃欲试的想法，那就去做吧。"],[57.13,62.4,16,"But scope it down to something you can finish and evaluate in about four weeks.","但请把范围收窄到大约四周内能完成并评测的程度。"],[62.75,68.76,16,"For your own topic, the optional one-page proposal is the best way to get early feedback.","如果是自拟题目，可选的一页提案是获得早期反馈的最好方式。"],[69.11,75.25,16,"Either way, the project guide page on the course website is your main reference, and I'll walk you through it now.","无论哪种方式，课程网站上的项目指南页面都是你的主要参考，我现在就带你们过一遍。"],[76.5,78.6,17,"Here are the eight tracks for this term.","这是本学期的八个方向。"],[78.95,87.37,17,"They're ordered from the most popular and easiest to get into, down to the more specialised ones, with competitions and entrepreneurship at the end.","它们按从最热门、最容易上手，到更专业的顺序排列，竞赛和创业放在最后。"],[87.72,94.53,17,"The most useful thing on this slide is the text in parentheses, because it tells you what compute you need.","这页最有用的是括号里的文字，因为它告诉你需要什么样的算力。"],[94.88,105.01,17,"If you only have API access or a laptop, look at A for agents, D for evaluation and datasets, and E for AI and society.","如果你只有 API 或一台笔记本，可以看 A 智能体、D 评测与数据集，以及 E AI 与社会。"],[105.36,111.28,17,"If you have a GPU, B, training your own model, and F, efficiency, open up.","如果你有 GPU，B 训练自己的模型和 F 效率优化也都可以考虑。"],[111.63,115.42,17,"C is for people who love building interactive demos.","C 适合喜欢做交互式演示的同学。"],[115.77,119.5,17,"G lets you use a competition as your project.","G 让你可以把一项竞赛作为你的项目。"],[119.85,125.66,17,"And H is for those who want to try a startup prototype with real users.","而 H 适合想用真实用户试一个创业原型的同学。"],[126.01,133.18,17,"Pick by two things: what resources you really have, and what you'd enjoy explaining at the poster session.","按两点来选：你真正拥有什么资源，以及你在海报展上乐于讲解什么。"],[134.43,137.29,18,"Here's a quick tour of how to use the project page.","下面快速介绍一下怎么用项目页面。"],[137.64,146.29,18,"Every brief has the same shape: a question, what to compare, what to measure, what to deliver, a four-week plan, and links.","每个简介结构都一样：一个问题、比较什么、测量什么、交付什么、一份四周计划，以及相关链接。"],[146.64,151.24,18,"There's a track finder that asks three questions and suggests two tracks.","页面上有一个方向推荐器，问你三个问题，然后推荐两个方向。"],[151.59,154.56,18,"And a compute filter hides the briefs you can't run.","还有一个算力筛选器，会隐藏你跑不了的课题。"],[154.91,159.03,18,"The page is bilingual; there's a Chinese button at the top right.","页面是中英双语的，右上角有一个中文按钮。"],[159.38,162.8,18,"Writing tips and samples are on a separate page.","写作建议和范例在另一个单独的页面上。"],[163.15,171.56,18,"The proposal template, report structure, reproducibility checklist and FAQ are at the end of the page.","提案模板、报告结构、可复现性清单和常见问题都在页面末尾。"],[171.91,176.05,18,"The line I most want you to remember is the rule of thumb at the bottom.","我最希望你们记住的，是最下面这条经验法则。"],[176.4,179.19,18,"One change: test one idea at a time.","一次只改一处：每次只检验一个想法。"],[179.54,185.57,18,"Matched budget: your method and the baseline get the same compute, tokens or model calls.","预算对齐：你的方法和基线使用相同的算力、token 数或模型调用次数。"],[185.92,189.29,18,"Held-out split: never tune on your test data.","留出集：永远不要在测试数据上调参。"],[189.64,193.12,18,"Independent checker: don't let the model grade its own work.","独立检查者：不要让模型给自己的作业打分。"],[193.47,195.71,18,"Seeds: run more than once.","随机种子：不要只跑一次。"],[196.06,200.61,18,"Replayable traces: log everything so someone can check it.","可回放的轨迹：把一切记录下来，方便别人核查。"],[200.96,204.48,18,"Follow those six, and your project will be sound.","做到这六条，你的项目就是严谨的。"],[205.73,212.47,19,"Let's go through the tracks, starting with Track A, agents and harness, which follows directly from last week's lecture.","我们逐个来看这些方向，先从 A 方向开始：智能体与 harness，它直接承接上周的课。"],[212.82,216.56,19,"The idea is that the harness itself is what you study.","核心思想是：harness 本身就是你的研究对象。"],[216.91,221.03,19,"Does a loop that sees real feedback beat simply generating once?","一个能看到真实反馈的循环，能否胜过只生成一次？"],[221.38,228.76,19,"By real feedback I mean error messages, test results, rendered images, or a simulator's measurements.","我说的真实反馈，是指报错信息、测试结果、渲染出的图像，或者模拟器的测量值。"],[229.11,232.97,19,"And critically, the comparison must be at a matched budget.","而且关键在于，比较必须在相同预算下进行。"],[233.32,240.31,19,"If your agent calls the model ten times, the baseline should get ten tries too; otherwise the comparison isn't fair.","如果你的智能体调用了模型十次，基线也应该有十次机会，否则比较就不公平。"],[240.66,245.01,19,"And you should report what each success costs.","你还应该报告每一次成功的成本。"],[245.36,248.61,19,"The briefs range from fun to serious.","这些课题从好玩的到严肃的都有。"],[248.96,256.07,19,"Drawing a pelican on a bicycle in three dot js with a hand-built harness, or building playable games.","用 three.js 加手工搭建的 harness 画一只骑自行车的鹈鹕，或者做出能玩的游戏。"],[256.42,264.5,19,"An agent that designs a machine against a simulator, repository repair, and program search on ARC-AGI.","在模拟器中设计机器的智能体、代码仓库修复，以及在 ARC-AGI 上做程序搜索。"],[264.85,269.36,19,"And new this year: Agent Skills, and agents that do research.","还有今年新增的：Agent Skills，以及做研究的智能体。"],[269.71,274.66,19,"Most of these only need an API model, which is why it's the most popular track.","这些课题大多只需要一个 API 模型，这也是它成为最热门方向的原因。"],[275.91,280.41,20,"If you want to build agent systems quickly, here are some open-source starting points.","如果你想快速搭建智能体系统，这里有一些开源的起点。"],[280.76,283.03,20,"Dify gives you a visual workflow builder.","Dify 提供了一个可视化的工作流构建器。"],[283.38,289.36,20,"You connect nodes for retrieval over your own corpora, MCP servers, and a hub of tools.","你可以连接各种节点：在自己的语料上做检索、MCP 服务器，以及一个工具中心。"],[289.71,294.02,20,"And you get a working application without writing much glue code.","不用写多少胶水代码，就能得到一个可用的应用。"],[294.37,301.31,20,"For more autonomous agents, OpenManus and OWL are open-source projects in the spirit of Manus.","如果想要更自主的智能体，OpenManus 和 OWL 是延续 Manus 思路的开源项目。"],[301.66,306.12,20,"There, the agent plans and executes multi-step tasks by itself.","在这些系统里，智能体会自己规划并执行多步任务。"],[306.47,311.89,20,"A word of caution: wiring these together is a starting point, not a research contribution.","提醒一句：把这些工具连起来只是起点，而不是研究贡献。"],[312.24,317.15,20,"Use them as a scaffold or a baseline, and then ask a question on top.","把它们当作脚手架或基线，然后在此之上提出一个问题。"],[317.5,323.69,20,"For example: does adding a verification step actually improve the success rate at the same cost?","比如：在相同成本下，加一个验证步骤真的能提高成功率吗？"],[324.94,328.72,21,"One idea I particularly like: build a new skill.","我特别喜欢的一个想法是：做一个新的 skill。"],[329.07,337.55,21,"In the sense of Agent Skills, a skill is basically a folder of instructions, and sometimes scripts, that an agent loads only when it needs it.","在 Agent Skills 的意义上，一个 skill 基本上就是一个装着指令、有时还有脚本的文件夹，智能体只在需要时才加载它。"],[337.9,344.84,21,"The example here is Frontend Slides, a skill for Claude Code that turns content into polished HTML slide decks.","这里的例子是 Frontend Slides，一个 Claude Code 的 skill，能把内容变成精美的 HTML 幻灯片。"],[345.19,350.24,21,"Someone had a recurring need, packaged the know-how as a skill, and shared it on GitHub.","有人有一个反复出现的需求，把相关经验打包成 skill，并分享到了 GitHub 上。"],[350.59,357.73,21,"As a project, the question becomes: can you build a skill for a real, recurring task, and show that it measurably helps?","作为项目，问题就变成：你能否为一个真实且反复出现的任务做一个 skill，并证明它带来了可量化的帮助？"],[358.08,365.13,21,"For instance, does the agent with your skill produce better output than without it, on a fixed set of tasks?","比如，在一组固定任务上，装了你的 skill 的智能体，输出是否比不装更好？"],[365.48,368.62,21,"And do real people actually install and use it?","真实用户会不会真的安装并使用它？"],[368.97,371.94,21,"That's brief A nine on the project page.","这就是项目页面上的课题 A9。"],[373.19,377.25,22,"Here's another agent-flavoured idea: let AI write the survey.","再来一个智能体风格的想法：让 AI 来写综述。"],[377.6,386.08,22,"AutoSurvey, a NeurIPS two thousand twenty-four paper, showed that an LLM pipeline can write a literature survey.","AutoSurvey 是 NeurIPS 2024 的一篇论文，它展示了大模型流水线可以撰写文献综述。"],[386.43,396.64,22,"It retrieves papers, generates an outline, drafts each subsection in parallel, then integrates, refines and evaluates the result.","它先检索论文、生成提纲，并行撰写各个小节，然后整合、润色并评估结果。"],[396.99,401.72,22,"The slide asks, half-jokingly: should you use Manus for your survey?","幻灯片半开玩笑地问：你要不要用 Manus 来写综述？"],[402.07,405.99,22,"You can try. But the research question is in the auditing.","你可以试试。但研究问题在于审核。"],[406.34,412.06,22,"Are the citations real? Does each claim actually match what the cited paper says?","引用是真实的吗？每个论断真的和被引论文说的一致吗？"],[412.41,415.98,22,"And how does it compare with a human-written survey?","它和人写的综述相比又如何？"],[416.33,421.97,22,"That's brief A ten: an agent writes the survey, and you audit it carefully.","这就是课题 A10：智能体写综述，你来仔细审核。"],[422.32,428.35,22,"Spoiler: you will find problems, and characterising them well is a perfectly good result.","剧透一下：你一定会发现问题，而把这些问题刻画清楚，本身就是很好的结果。"],[429.6,433.84,23,"Track B is for those who want to get their hands dirty with training.","B 方向适合想亲自动手做训练的同学。"],[434.19,437.1,23,"The motto is: to understand it, build it.","座右铭是：要理解它，就去构建它。"],[437.45,443.71,23,"The method is always the same: change one thing at a fixed token or compute budget, and plot the curve.","方法始终如一：在固定的 token 或算力预算下只改一处，然后画出曲线。"],[444.06,445.65,23,"There are several flavours.","这里有几种不同的做法。"],[446.0,452.97,23,"You can pre-train a small model from scratch, in the zero point one to zero point five billion parameter range.","你可以从零预训练一个小模型，参数规模在 0.1B 到 0.5B 之间。"],[453.32,461.49,23,"New this year is the nanoGPT speedrun, a community effort to train a small GPT to a target loss as fast as possible.","今年新增的是 nanoGPT speedrun，这是一项社区活动，目标是尽可能快地把一个小 GPT 训练到目标损失。"],[461.84,465.3,23,"There, you try one architecture change at matched time.","在这里，你在相同的时间内尝试一处架构改动。"],[465.65,475.04,23,"You can also apply the Tutorial two recipe to a vertical domain: continued pre-training, SFT, then DPO or GRPO, plus RAG.","你也可以把 Tutorial 2 的配方用到一个垂直领域：继续预训练、SFT，然后 DPO 或 GRPO，再加上 RAG。"],[475.39,481.74,23,"Or attach a new modality, like speech, ECG or time series, to an LLM.","或者给大模型接入一种新模态，比如语音、心电图或时间序列。"],[482.09,483.75,23,"You'll need a GPU for this one.","这个方向需要 GPU。"],[484.1,489.37,23,"And if you're interested in Huawei Ascend NPUs, mention it in your proposal.","如果你对华为昇腾 NPU 感兴趣，请在提案里注明。"],[490.62,498.2,24,"Let me show you what a vertical model looks like, with an example from our own lab: HuatuoGPT, a medical LLM.","我用我们实验室的一个例子来展示垂直模型是什么样的：医疗大模型 HuatuoGPT。"],[498.55,500.39,24,"Look at the four boxes on the left.","看左边这四个方框。"],[500.74,507.61,24,"The data comes from two sources: distilled from ChatGPT, and real-world data from doctors.","数据有两个来源：从 ChatGPT 蒸馏的数据，以及来自医生的真实世界数据。"],[507.96,513.33,24,"And it comes in two formats: single-turn instructions, and multi-turn conversations.","数据有两种形式：单轮指令和多轮对话。"],[513.68,517.68,24,"The distilled data makes the model fluent and patient-friendly.","蒸馏数据让模型表达流畅、对患者友好。"],[518.03,524.9,24,"The real doctor data makes it behave more like a doctor, for example asking follow-up questions before diagnosing.","真实医生数据让它表现得更像医生，比如在诊断前先追问。"],[525.25,533.45,24,"After SFT on this mix, a second stage uses feedback from both ChatGPT and doctors to align the model further.","在这批混合数据上做完 SFT 之后，第二阶段再利用 ChatGPT 和医生双方的反馈进一步对齐模型。"],[533.8,540.31,24,"The lesson for your project: in a vertical model, the data recipe is the main design decision.","对你的项目的启示是：在垂直模型里，数据配方才是最主要的设计决策。"],[540.66,548.35,24,"HuatuoGPT-II, the second link, pushed this further with a simpler domain-adaptation recipe.","第二个链接 HuatuoGPT-II 更进一步，用了更简单的领域适配配方。"],[549.6,554.59,25,"And the same pattern works in many domains. Here are a few more examples.","同样的模式在很多领域都适用。再看几个例子。"],[554.94,562.78,25,"ORLM, for optimization modelling, turns a natural-language business problem into a mathematical model a solver can run.","ORLM 面向优化建模，把用自然语言描述的业务问题转化成求解器可以运行的数学模型。"],[563.13,565.87,25,"GrammarGPT is for grammatical error correction.","GrammarGPT 用于语法纠错。"],[566.22,570.62,25,"BlenderLLM writes Blender scripts to produce CAD models.","BlenderLLM 编写 Blender 脚本来生成 CAD 模型。"],[570.97,576.48,25,"And RAG-Instruct builds instruction data to make models better at using retrieved documents.","RAG-Instruct 则构建指令数据，让模型更善于利用检索到的文档。"],[576.83,578.99,25,"Each one follows the same formula.","它们都遵循同一个公式。"],[579.34,589.15,25,"Pick a domain where general models are weak, build or curate a dataset for it, fine-tune, and evaluate with a benchmark that domain experts would trust.","选一个通用模型表现薄弱的领域，为它构建或整理数据集，微调，再用领域专家认可的基准来评测。"],[589.5,598.49,25,"If you come from engineering, finance, law or any other field, ask yourself where general LLMs disappoint you in that field.","如果你来自工程、金融、法律或其他领域，问问自己：通用大模型在你的领域里哪里让你失望？"],[598.84,600.63,25,"That might be your project.","那可能就是你的项目。"],[601.88,607.53,26,"Language is another kind of vertical. Here's our work on Arabic LLMs.","语言是另一种垂直领域。这是我们在阿拉伯语大模型上的工作。"],[607.88,612.05,26,"AceGPT was about localising an LLM to Arabic.","AceGPT 是把大模型本地化到阿拉伯语。"],[612.4,619.6,26,"And not just the language, but the cultural values, so the model answers the way an Arabic-speaking user would find appropriate.","不仅是语言，还有文化价值观，让模型的回答方式让阿拉伯语用户觉得得体。"],[619.95,627.71,26,"AceGPT one point five studied vocabulary expansion: how to add Arabic tokens to the tokenizer progressively.","AceGPT 1.5 研究的是词表扩展：如何把阿拉伯语 token 逐步加入分词器。"],[628.06,631.17,26,"A bit like how a person learns a second language.","有点像一个人学习第二语言的过程。"],[631.52,639.86,26,"And AceGPT two moved alignment into pre-training itself, which we called native alignment, published at NeurIPS two thousand twenty-four.","AceGPT 2 把对齐放进了预训练本身，我们称之为原生对齐，发表在 NeurIPS 2024。"],[640.21,648.0,26,"The takeaway for you is brief B seven: adapt a model to a language or dialect, and measure what it forgets along the way.","对你们的启示就是课题 B7：把模型适配到某种语言或方言，并测量它在这个过程中遗忘了什么。"],[648.35,654.37,26,"If your hometown dialect is under-served by current models, that's a meaningful project.","如果你家乡的方言没有被现有模型很好地支持，那就是一个很有意义的项目。"],[655.62,662.24,27,"Another example from our lab, this time adding a new modality: speech. The paper is Soundwave.","再看我们实验室的另一个例子，这次是加入一种新模态：语音。论文叫 Soundwave。"],[662.59,664.47,27,"Look at the radar chart on the right.","看右边的雷达图。"],[664.82,669.53,27,"The pink area is Soundwave, trained on about ten thousand hours of speech.","粉色区域是 Soundwave，用了大约一万小时的语音训练。"],[669.88,675.39,27,"The purple area is Qwen2-Audio, trained on about half a million hours.","紫色区域是 Qwen2-Audio，用了大约五十万小时。"],[675.74,682.15,27,"With roughly one-fiftieth of the data, Soundwave matches or beats it on most of these tasks.","Soundwave 只用了大约五十分之一的数据，却在大多数任务上追平甚至超越了它。"],[682.5,686.76,27,"Speech grounding, emotion recognition, speaker counting, and so on.","比如语音定位、情绪识别、说话人计数等等。"],[687.11,688.87,27,"How? Two things.","怎么做到的？两点。"],[689.22,694.32,27,"An extra CTC loss that helps align speech representations with text.","一是额外加入的 CTC 损失，帮助语音表示与文本对齐。"],[694.67,697.6,27,"And much more careful data engineering.","二是精细得多的数据工程。"],[697.95,703.19,27,"The message I want you to take away: you don't need industrial-scale data to do something interesting.","我希望你们记住的是：做有意思的工作，并不需要工业级规模的数据。"],[703.54,707.54,27,"A good idea and clean data can win on an academic budget.","一个好点子加上干净的数据，在学术预算下也能取胜。"],[708.79,710.72,28,"A short note on hardware.","简单说一下硬件。"],[711.07,714.59,28,"We have some connection with Huawei Ascend, the NPU family.","我们和华为昇腾，也就是那个 NPU 系列，有一些合作联系。"],[714.94,720.56,28,"Adapting training or inference to Ascend is itself a legitimate engineering project.","把训练或推理适配到昇腾上，本身就是一个正当的工程项目。"],[720.91,725.72,28,"Port a model, check that it produces the same outputs, and measure the speed.","移植一个模型，检查它是否产生相同的输出，再测量速度。"],[726.07,730.98,28,"We might be able to share some NPU access later, but I can't promise it yet.","之后我们也许能分享一些 NPU 资源，但现在还不能保证。"],[731.33,735.78,28,"If you're interested, say so in your proposal, and we'll see what we can do.","如果你感兴趣，请在提案里说明，我们看看能做些什么。"]]},{"n":3,"title":"Interactive Systems, Evaluation and Datasets","blurb":"Track C on 3D, VR, digital humans and education, with special topics from our lab, then Track D on evaluation, rubrics, datasets and retrieval.","file":"lecture08_part3.mp4","poster":"lecture08_part3.jpg","duration":656.3,"first":29,"last":41,"slides":[{"n":29,"title":"Track C: HCI: 3D/VR worlds, digital humans, education & interaction","t":0.8},{"n":30,"title":"HCI Applications and Agent","t":65.76},{"n":31,"title":"Slide 31","t":110.97},{"n":32,"title":"Track C (part 2) examples: applications in education","t":156.19},{"n":33,"title":"Special Topic","t":204.22},{"n":34,"title":"Special Topic","t":249.77},{"n":35,"title":"Happy-Medical-AI","t":286.37},{"n":36,"title":"Track D: Evaluation, datasets & evidence","t":340.86},{"n":37,"title":"https://openrouter.ai/models?q=qwen","t":406.04},{"n":38,"title":"Examples","t":446.34},{"n":39,"title":"Rubrics-based Evaluations","t":492.8},{"n":40,"title":"Examples","t":552.15},{"n":41,"title":"Retrieval and RAG","t":601.42}],"sents":[[0.8,5.9,29,"Track C is human-computer interaction, and it's the most visual track.","C 方向是人机交互，也是最直观、最有视觉效果的方向。"],[6.25,10.52,29,"The idea is that interaction itself is the variable you study.","核心思想是：交互本身就是你研究的变量。"],[10.87,19.73,29,"Part one puts an LLM inside something: a 3D scene, a game, a VR headset, a robot simulator, or an animated character.","第一部分是把大模型放进某个东西里：3D 场景、游戏、VR 头显、机器人模拟器，或者动画角色。"],[20.08,26.16,29,"The questions are about spatial language, memory, grounded action, and real-time decisions.","研究问题涉及空间语言、记忆、具身行动和实时决策。"],[26.51,33.98,29,"Part two is about education: turning a piece of teaching material into something a learner can watch, rotate or run.","第二部分关于教育：把一份教学材料变成学习者可以观看、旋转或运行的东西。"],[34.33,39.45,29,"And asking when an assistant should ask, remember, or stay quiet.","并探究助手什么时候该提问、该记住，或者该保持沉默。"],[39.8,44.2,29,"Look at the subtitle: fidelity and transfer, not engagement.","看副标题：保真度和迁移，而不是参与度。"],[44.55,47.58,29,"A flashy demo that people enjoy is not enough.","一个大家玩得开心的炫酷演示是不够的。"],[47.93,54.02,29,"We want to know whether the character behaves correctly, and whether learners actually learn something that transfers.","我们想知道角色的行为是否正确，学习者是否真的学到了可以迁移的东西。"],[54.37,64.36,29,"So plan a real evaluation: a scripted fidelity check and a transfer task, or a small user study with a pre-test and a post-test.","所以请规划一个真正的评测：脚本化的保真度检查加一个迁移任务，或者一个带前测和后测的小型用户研究。"],[65.61,68.38,30,"Here's a fun one: an AI campus.","来看一个好玩的：AI 校园。"],[68.73,73.2,30,"What you're seeing is a blocky, game-style reconstruction of a campus.","你看到的是一个方块风格、游戏式的校园复刻。"],[73.55,80.9,30,"The idea behind brief C one is to fill a virtual CUHK-Shenzhen with NPCs driven by LLMs.","课题 C1 的想法，是在一个虚拟的港中深里放满由大模型驱动的 NPC。"],[81.25,89.71,30,"You may know the Generative Agents paper from Stanford, where little agents lived in a small town, had memories, and planned their days.","你可能知道斯坦福的 Generative Agents 论文，里面的小智能体生活在一个小镇上，拥有记忆，还会规划自己的一天。"],[90.06,91.92,30,"Imagine that on our own campus.","想象一下把它搬到我们自己的校园。"],[92.27,98.85,30,"An NPC librarian who remembers what you asked last week, or students who organise an event together.","一个记得你上周问过什么的 NPC 图书管理员，或者一起组织活动的学生们。"],[99.2,103.24,30,"The research questions are about memory and spatial understanding.","研究问题关于记忆和空间理解。"],[103.59,109.57,30,"For example, can the agent follow an instruction like: meet me at the library next to the lake?","比如，智能体能否听懂这样的指令：在湖边的图书馆跟我碰头？"],[110.82,115.75,31,"This screenshot is Dify's workflow editor again, which I mentioned under agents.","这张截图又是 Dify 的工作流编辑器，我在讲智能体时提到过它。"],[116.1,122.8,31,"I'm showing it here because many of these interactive demos are glued together with exactly this kind of tool.","我在这里再展示它，是因为很多交互式演示正是用这类工具拼接起来的。"],[123.15,123.99,31,"Look at the flow.","看这个流程。"],[124.34,128.58,31,"A question classifier routes the user's query into different branches.","一个问题分类器把用户的提问分流到不同的分支。"],[128.93,135.15,31,"Each branch retrieves from its own knowledge base, and then an LLM node generates the answer.","每个分支从自己的知识库中检索，然后由一个大模型节点生成答案。"],[135.5,140.43,31,"And there's a fallback, a direct answer, when the question is out of scope.","当问题超出范围时，还有一个兜底的直接回复。"],[140.78,149.59,31,"For an NPC or a tutor, that's a sensible architecture: classify what the user wants, retrieve the right context, then respond.","对于 NPC 或辅导助手，这是一个合理的架构：先判断用户想要什么，再检索合适的上下文，然后回应。"],[149.94,154.79,31,"Prototype it visually first, then optimise the parts that matter.","先用可视化方式做出原型，再去优化真正关键的部分。"],[156.04,160.54,32,"Part two of Track C is education, and there are lots of possibilities here.","C 方向的第二部分是教育，这里有很多可能性。"],[160.89,164.43,32,"You could build an assistant for online classroom teaching.","你可以做一个在线课堂教学的助手。"],[164.78,171.95,32,"You could let students talk to historical figures, say, interview a famous scientist about their discoveries.","你可以让学生和历史人物对话，比如采访一位著名科学家，聊聊他的发现。"],[172.3,178.1,32,"You could create visualisations for math, where an abstract concept becomes an animation.","你可以为数学做可视化，把抽象概念变成动画。"],[178.45,188.59,32,"Or virtual experiments with real-time interaction in physics, chemistry or medicine, where a student can change a parameter and see what happens.","或者做物理、化学或医学的实时交互虚拟实验，让学生改一个参数，看看会发生什么。"],[188.94,193.18,32,"The hard part is never the demo; it's showing that it helps learning.","难点从来不是演示，而是证明它真的有助于学习。"],[193.53,202.82,32,"A good education project compares two versions, for example with and without your tool, and measures what students actually understand afterwards.","一个好的教育项目会比较两个版本，比如用和不用你的工具，并测量学生之后真正理解了多少。"],[204.07,209.91,33,"A special topic I'm fond of: AI for babies, or for complete newcomers.","一个我很喜欢的特别话题：给婴儿，或者给完全零基础的人讲 AI。"],[210.26,214.21,33,"You may have seen the Quantum Physics for Babies picture books by Chris Ferrie.","你也许见过 Chris Ferrie 写的绘本《给宝宝的量子物理》。"],[214.56,219.26,33,"They explain a hard topic in a few simple pictures and sentences.","它用几幅简单的图和几句话，讲清楚一个很难的话题。"],[219.61,226.31,33,"Could you make a picture book that explains AI in the same way, with pictures and text, perhaps generated with AI help?","你能否用同样的方式做一本解释 AI 的绘本，图文并茂，也许还借助 AI 来生成？"],[226.66,228.46,33,"It's harder than it sounds.","这比听起来要难。"],[228.81,235.05,33,"You have to simplify without saying anything false, and keep the illustrations consistent from page to page.","你得在简化的同时不说错任何东西，还要让插图在每一页之间保持一致。"],[235.4,244.56,33,"And then test it with real readers, like parents reading it to their kids, or friends with no technical background, to see whether they get it.","然后找真实读者来测试，比如给孩子读绘本的家长，或者没有技术背景的朋友，看看他们能不能看懂。"],[244.91,248.37,33,"Making something simple and correct is a real skill.","把东西做得既简单又正确，是一项真本事。"],[249.62,257.65,34,"Along the same lines, here's a successful example of educational content: Happy-LLM, by the Datawhale community.","沿着同样的思路，这是一个成功的教育内容案例：Datawhale 社区的 Happy-LLM。"],[258.0,265.21,34,"It's an open-source tutorial in Chinese that takes you from the basics all the way to building a large language model from scratch.","这是一个中文开源教程，带你从基础一路走到从零构建一个大语言模型。"],[265.56,268.54,34,"And it has become very popular on GitHub.","它在 GitHub 上非常受欢迎。"],[268.89,272.83,34,"A tutorial like this can be a project too, if it's done seriously.","这样的教程，只要认真做，也可以成为一个项目。"],[273.18,277.69,34,"The deliverable is the material itself, plus some evidence that it works.","交付物是教材本身，加上一些证明它有效的证据。"],[278.04,284.97,34,"Learners who completed it, exercises they could solve, and feedback you collected and acted on.","比如完成学习的人数、他们能解出的练习，以及你收集并据此改进的反馈。"],[286.22,293.72,35,"And here's one from our own group, Happy-Medical-AI. It's an open tutorial on AI in medicine, in Chinese.","这是我们自己课题组的一个项目：Happy-Medical-AI。它是一个关于医学 AI 的中文开放教程。"],[294.07,296.58,35,"Look at the chapter structure in the table.","看表格中的章节结构。"],[296.93,302.77,35,"It starts with an overview of AI applications in medicine, and how general and medical models differ.","它从 AI 在医疗中的应用概览，以及通用模型和医疗模型的区别讲起。"],[303.12,307.6,35,"Then prompt engineering for general models in clinical scenarios.","然后是在临床场景中为通用模型做提示词工程。"],[307.95,312.51,35,"Then generalist medical assistants like HuatuoGPT.","接着是像 HuatuoGPT 这样的全科医疗助手。"],[312.86,319.3,35,"Then specialist models, such as XrayGPT for X-rays and OncoGPT for oncology.","再是专科模型，比如用于 X 光片的 XrayGPT 和用于肿瘤的 OncoGPT。"],[319.65,323.76,35,"And finally, real hospital deployment cases and their challenges.","最后是真实的医院落地案例及其挑战。"],[324.11,329.04,35,"If you'd like to make educational content for a specific field, this is a good template.","如果你想为某个特定领域做教育内容，这是一个很好的模板。"],[329.39,334.42,35,"A clear progression, real examples, and an honest look at limitations.","循序渐进的结构、真实的案例，以及对局限的坦诚审视。"],[334.77,339.46,35,"That brings us from teaching people to measuring models, which is Track D.","这就把我们从教人带到了测量模型，也就是 D 方向。"],[340.71,344.83,36,"Track D is evaluation, datasets and evidence.","D 方向是评测、数据集与证据。"],[345.18,353.76,36,"The one-line definition is worth remembering: a benchmark is a dataset with a scoring rule. Both halves matter.","这句一行定义值得记住：基准就是带评分规则的数据集。两半都很重要。"],[354.11,360.21,36,"Part one is about building evaluations that expose a specific failure of the strongest models.","第一部分是构建评测，揭示最强模型的某种具体失败。"],[360.56,367.3,36,"In culture, humour, logic, long context, prompt injection, or detecting machine-written text.","比如在文化、幽默、逻辑、长上下文、提示注入，或识别机器生成文本等方面。"],[367.65,372.18,36,"Ideally, they're scored with rubrics written by domain experts.","理想情况下，用领域专家撰写的评分细则来打分。"],[372.53,377.57,36,"Part two builds the things that training and retrieval depend on.","第二部分是构建训练和检索所依赖的东西。"],[377.92,385.01,36,"Datasets for a specific training stage, corpora with documented sources, and auditable evidence chains.","面向特定训练阶段的数据集、来源有据可查的语料，以及可审计的证据链。"],[385.36,389.73,36,"Look at the subtitle: human baseline, provenance, licences.","看副标题：人类基线、数据来源、许可协议。"],[390.08,393.77,36,"Have humans take your test so we know what good looks like.","让人类也做一遍你的测试，这样我们才知道好的水平是什么样。"],[394.12,398.94,36,"Record where every item came from, and check that you're allowed to use the data.","记录每一条数据的来源，并确认你有权使用这些数据。"],[399.29,404.64,36,"Most of this track runs on APIs or a CPU, so it's very accessible.","这个方向大多只需 API 或 CPU，门槛很低。"],[405.89,410.36,37,"A practical tip for anyone evaluating many models: OpenRouter.","给需要评测很多模型的同学一个实用建议：OpenRouter。"],[410.71,417.15,37,"It gives you one API, in the OpenAI format, to call hundreds of models from different providers.","它提供一个 OpenAI 格式的 API，让你调用来自不同厂商的数百个模型。"],[417.5,425.5,37,"Here I've searched for Qwen, and you can see several models listed with their context lengths and prices per million tokens.","这里我搜索了 Qwen，你可以看到列出的几个模型，以及它们的上下文长度和每百万 token 的价格。"],[425.85,427.15,37,"Some are even free.","有些甚至是免费的。"],[427.5,433.24,37,"For an evaluation project, that means you can compare ten models without opening ten accounts.","对评测项目来说，这意味着你不用注册十个账号就能比较十个模型。"],[433.59,437.45,37,"Two cautions. First, set a spending limit before you start.","两点提醒。第一，开始之前先设好消费上限。"],[437.8,444.94,37,"Second, record the exact model versions and dates, because hosted models change over time.","第二，记录确切的模型版本和日期，因为托管的模型会随时间变化。"],[446.19,453.26,38,"Here's a list of benchmarks, many from our lab and our collaborators, to show you how broad this space is.","这是一份基准列表，很多来自我们实验室和合作者，让你们看看这个领域有多广。"],[453.61,458.68,38,"There are benchmarks for fresh, up-to-date knowledge, and for speech-to-speech systems.","有针对最新知识的基准，也有针对语音到语音系统的基准。"],[459.03,463.47,38,"User-centric evaluation, and professional medical QA.","以用户为中心的评测，以及专业医学问答。"],[463.82,467.55,38,"Olympiad-level math, and long multi-image contexts.","奥赛级别的数学，以及长的多图上下文。"],[467.9,472.47,38,"Mathematical modelling, Arabic culture, and multimodal LLMs.","数学建模、阿拉伯文化，以及多模态大模型。"],[472.82,476.99,38,"I won't go through them one by one; you can find each on Google Scholar.","我不逐个讲了，每一个都可以在 Google Scholar 上找到。"],[477.34,482.89,38,"The point is that a good benchmark can be a complete, publishable project in itself.","重点是，一个好的基准本身就可以是一个完整、可发表的项目。"],[483.24,491.4,38,"What they have in common is a clear claim about what current models can't yet do, and a careful, defensible way of measuring it.","它们的共同点是：明确指出当前模型还做不到什么，并用一种严谨、站得住脚的方式去测量。"],[492.65,500.62,39,"One evaluation idea that has become very important is rubric-based evaluation. This is from OpenAI's HealthBench.","有一种评测思路已经变得非常重要：基于评分细则的评测。这个例子来自 OpenAI 的 HealthBench。"],[500.97,502.61,39,"Look at the three columns.","看这三栏。"],[502.96,510.11,39,"On the left is a user's question: a seventy-year-old neighbour is lying on the floor, unresponsive but breathing.","左边是用户的问题：一位 70 岁的邻居躺在地上，没有反应，但还有呼吸。"],[510.46,512.28,39,"In the middle is a model's answer.","中间是模型的回答。"],[512.63,518.65,39,"On the right is a rubric written by physicians: a list of criteria, each worth some points.","右边是医生撰写的评分细则：一系列标准，每条各有分值。"],[519.0,526.07,39,"Does it tell you to call emergency services? Does it say so at the beginning? Does it advise CPR if there's no pulse?","它有没有让你呼叫急救？有没有在开头就这么说？没有脉搏时有没有建议做心肺复苏？"],[526.42,532.12,39,"A grader checks each criterion, and the score is points earned over the maximum.","评分者逐条检查，得分就是所得分数除以满分。"],[532.47,537.2,39,"Here, it's seventy-one out of ninety-two, about seventy-seven percent.","这里是 92 分里得了 71 分，大约 77%。"],[537.55,544.73,39,"Why does this matter? For open-ended answers there's no single gold answer, but experts can say what a good answer must contain.","为什么这很重要？开放式回答没有唯一的标准答案，但专家可以说出好答案必须包含什么。"],[545.08,550.75,39,"And those same rubrics can be turned into rewards for RL, which is brief D eight.","而且这些评分细则还能转化为强化学习的奖励，这就是课题 D8。"],[552.0,554.85,40,"Datasets are the other half of Track D.","数据集是 D 方向的另一半。"],[555.2,564.57,40,"A few examples: Huatuo-26M, a large-scale Chinese medical question-answering dataset from our lab.","举几个例子：Huatuo-26M，我们实验室的大规模中文医疗问答数据集。"],[564.92,571.38,40,"Med Pajama, and VLFeedback, a dataset of AI feedback for aligning vision-language models.","Med Pajama，以及 VLFeedback，一个用于对齐视觉语言模型的 AI 反馈数据集。"],[571.73,575.86,40,"A dataset project is a real contribution if it's done properly.","数据集项目只要做得扎实，就是真正的贡献。"],[576.21,584.16,40,"That means a clear collection process, deduplication and quality filtering, and documented sources and licences.","这意味着清晰的采集流程、去重和质量过滤，以及有据可查的来源和许可。"],[584.51,589.72,40,"Plus a demonstration that training or evaluating on it actually changes something.","再加上证明：用它训练或评测，确实带来了改变。"],[590.07,597.02,40,"Brief D thirteen asks you to build a training dataset for one specific stage, in the right format.","课题 D13 要求你为某一个特定训练阶段，按正确的格式构建训练数据集。"],[597.37,600.02,40,"That's a very concrete four-week project.","这是一个非常具体的四周项目。"],[601.27,606.59,41,"Retrieval and RAG fit naturally into this track too. Here are a few directions.","检索和 RAG 也很自然地属于这个方向。这里有几个思路。"],[606.94,611.97,41,"Better retrieval models for general or specific domains, for example math.","为通用或特定领域打造更好的检索模型，比如数学。"],[612.32,618.4,41,"Perhaps trained with synthesised hard negatives, which are passages that look relevant but aren't.","也许可以用合成的难负例来训练，也就是看似相关、实则无关的段落。"],[618.75,624.9,41,"Hallucination detection, where the system warns the user when an answer isn't supported by the sources.","幻觉检测：当答案得不到来源支持时，系统会提醒用户。"],[625.25,627.59,41,"And replicating OpenEvidence.","还有复现 OpenEvidence。"],[627.94,636.33,41,"The screenshot shows OpenEvidence, a medical search engine, answering a clinical question about choline supplementation during pregnancy.","截图展示的是医学搜索引擎 OpenEvidence，在回答一个关于孕期补充胆碱的临床问题。"],[636.68,641.2,41,"Notice that every claim has a numbered citation to a real paper.","注意，每个论断都带有编号引用，指向一篇真实的论文。"],[641.55,645.87,41,"Can you build something similar, with an open model and an open corpus?","你能否用开放模型和开放语料，做出类似的东西？"],[646.22,650.4,41,"And can you measure how often the citations really support the claims?","你能否测量这些引用有多大比例真正支持了对应的论断？"],[650.75,654.46,41,"That's an ambitious but very valuable project.","这是一个有野心、但非常有价值的项目。"]]},{"n":4,"title":"Society, Efficiency, Competitions and Startups","blurb":"Track E on position papers and audits, Track F on efficiency and kernels, Track G competitions, and Track H AI startups, with two real student startups from our campus.","file":"lecture08_part4.mp4","poster":"lecture08_part4.jpg","duration":477.0,"first":42,"last":50,"slides":[{"n":42,"title":"Track E: AI for society: position papers, audits & interventions","t":0.8},{"n":43,"title":"Track E reading: top-venue starting points by question","t":52.51},{"n":44,"title":"Track F: Efficiency, on-device & GPU kernels","t":99.2},{"n":45,"title":"Track G: Competitions: a formal final-project option","t":158.83},{"n":46,"title":"Track H: AI entrepreneurship: run a startup prototype","t":221.7},{"n":47,"title":"AI startup basics every founder in Track H should explain","t":276.54},{"n":48,"title":"For startups: FriesAI for classroom learning","t":346.93},{"n":49,"title":"截至2025年4月12日13点30分，薯塔AI已覆盖港中深60%的本科生，港中深注册人数达3579人，总注册人数达4680人。其中日活跃用户为1239人，平均每日AI问答数2898条。薯塔AI目前正在逐步推广至其他七所中外合办院校，进一步提","t":392.84},{"n":50,"title":"For startups","t":439.95}],"sents":[[0.8,4.95,42,"Track E moves from models to society, and it needs no GPU at all.","E 方向从模型转向社会，完全不需要 GPU。"],[5.3,9.27,42,"The subtitle says: a falsifiable claim and an honest test.","副标题写着：一个可证伪的论断，加一个诚实的检验。"],[9.62,11.77,42,"You take a position on one question.","你要在一个问题上表明立场。"],[12.12,17.31,42,"Does AI widen gender inequality? Does it serve minority languages and dialects worse?","AI 是否扩大了性别不平等？它对少数民族语言和方言的服务是否更差？"],[17.66,23.96,42,"Does it exclude people with disabilities? Does it leave the Global South behind, or concentrate wealth?","它是否把残障人士排除在外？是否让全球南方掉队，或者让财富更加集中？"],[24.31,28.28,42,"Then you back your position with a measurement you ran yourself.","然后用你自己做的测量来支撑你的立场。"],[28.63,31.9,42,"A classic method is the matched-persona audit.","一种经典方法是匹配人设审计。"],[32.25,42.13,42,"Ask exactly the same question, change only one attribute of the user, such as gender or dialect, and measure whether the answers differ.","问完全相同的问题，只改变用户的一个属性，比如性别或方言，然后测量回答是否不同。"],[42.48,51.11,42,"The output can be written like a position paper at ICML or NeurIPS, an audit, or an intervention you build and test with real users.","成果可以写成 ICML 或 NeurIPS 风格的立场论文，也可以是一份审计，或者一个你构建并与真实用户一起测试的干预方案。"],[52.36,55.94,43,"For Track E, here's a reading list grouped by question.","这是 E 方向按问题分组的阅读清单。"],[56.29,64.89,43,"Gender, minority languages and dialects, disability, the Global South, wealth and work, and pluralism and values.","性别、少数民族语言与方言、残障、全球南方、财富与工作，以及多元与价值观。"],[65.24,70.5,43,"All are from top venues like Nature, Science, ACL, FAccT and ICML.","它们都来自顶级期刊和会议，比如 Nature、Science、ACL、FAccT 和 ICML。"],[70.85,72.69,43,"Please don't try to read them all.","请不要试图全部读完。"],[73.04,78.47,43,"Pick the one question you care about, and read two or three papers in that row.","选一个你关心的问题，读那一行里的两三篇论文就好。"],[78.82,90.37,43,"For example, Hofmann and colleagues, in Nature two thousand twenty-four, showed that language models judge people more negatively based only on the dialect they write in.","例如，Hofmann 等人 2024 年在 Nature 上发表的研究表明，仅凭一个人书写所用的方言，语言模型就会对其作出更负面的评判。"],[90.72,95.71,43,"Notice how such papers make one sharp claim, and design one clean test for it.","注意这类论文是如何提出一个鲜明的论断，并为它设计一个干净的检验的。"],[96.06,97.8,43,"That's the style you should aim for.","这就是你们应该追求的风格。"],[99.05,104.18,44,"Track F is efficiency: making LLMs faster, cheaper and smaller.","F 方向是效率：让大模型更快、更便宜、更小。"],[104.53,111.64,44,"One GPU, or even a phone, and a careful measurement protocol can produce numbers worth publishing.","一块 GPU，甚至一部手机，加上严谨的测量方案，就能得出值得发表的数据。"],[111.99,118.2,44,"The topics include generating GPU kernels with feedback, evaluated on KernelBench.","题目包括借助反馈生成 GPU kernel，并在 KernelBench 上评测。"],[118.55,127.68,44,"Serving mixes of short and long requests, the real cost of quantization and distillation, speculative decoding across domains, and prefix caching.","还有长短请求混合服务、量化和蒸馏的真实代价、跨领域的推测解码，以及前缀缓存。"],[128.03,138.07,44,"New this year are an on-device protocol for phones and laptops, and an evolutionary loop that optimises your own kernel against a sealed test.","今年新增的是面向手机和笔记本的端侧测评方案，以及一个在封闭测试下优化你自己 kernel 的进化式循环。"],[138.42,142.18,44,"Note the subtitle: fresh-input correctness checks.","注意副标题：用全新输入做正确性检查。"],[142.53,150.3,44,"A generated kernel that's fast but wrong is worthless, and models are good at producing code that passes the visible tests.","一个又快又错的生成 kernel 毫无价值，而模型很擅长写出能通过可见测试的代码。"],[150.65,153.3,44,"Always verify on new random inputs.","一定要用新的随机输入来验证。"],[153.65,157.43,44,"We'll cover the background in Lecture eleven, on efficiency.","相关背景我们会在第十一讲“效率”中讲到。"],[158.68,162.78,45,"Track G makes competitions a formal final-project option.","G 方向把竞赛正式纳入期末项目的选项。"],[163.13,168.88,45,"You use a contest's task, dataset or simulator to answer a research question for the course.","你用比赛的任务、数据集或模拟器，来回答一个课程研究问题。"],[169.23,176.24,45,"The important line is the subtitle: the comparison is the grade. The leaderboard is a bonus.","关键在副标题：对比实验才是成绩，排行榜只是锦上添花。"],[176.59,181.88,45,"What we assess is the controlled comparison you ran on your own held-out split.","我们评估的是你在自己的留出集上做的受控对比。"],[182.23,190.48,45,"So register a course plan saying which contest, which metric, and what change you'll test, then submit the normal course deliverables on time.","所以请登记一份课程计划，写明哪个比赛、哪个指标、要检验什么改动，然后按时提交常规的课程材料。"],[190.83,198.02,45,"A contest whose final deadline falls after December twenty-fifth is fine, as long as your course deliverables are on time.","比赛的最终截止日期晚于 12 月 25 日也没关系，只要你的课程材料按时提交。"],[198.37,207.21,45,"The slide lists current Chinese and international contests, with dates checked on November third, plus archived benchmarks you can run locally.","幻灯片列出了当前的国内和国际比赛，日期核对于 11 月 3 日，还有可以在本地运行的往期基准。"],[207.56,213.33,45,"Two practical warnings. First, read the clause about which models are allowed before you start.","两条实用提醒。第一，开始之前先读清楚关于允许使用哪些模型的条款。"],[213.68,220.3,45,"Second, if real-name registration is needed, do it in week one, because it can take days.","第二，如果需要实名注册，请在第一周就办好，因为可能要花好几天。"],[221.55,227.8,46,"Track H is AI entrepreneurship: run a prototype of a startup with real users.","H 方向是 AI 创业：用真实用户运行一个创业原型。"],[228.15,232.45,46,"Notice the subtitle: retention and cost, not a pitch deck.","注意副标题：留存和成本，而不是路演 PPT。"],[232.8,234.26,46,"Anyone can make slides.","谁都能做幻灯片。"],[234.61,240.7,46,"We want to know whether real people come back to use your product, and what it costs you to serve them.","我们想知道真实用户会不会回来继续用你的产品，以及服务他们要花多少成本。"],[241.05,250.75,46,"The examples include an AI CEO running a tiny business, an AI seller, an AI tutor, and expertise training with simulated patients.","例子包括经营一家小生意的 AI CEO、AI 销售、AI 家教，以及用模拟病人做专业训练。"],[251.1,256.93,46,"There's also an AI game designer, open-world AI with VR, and speech-based 3D printing.","还有 AI 游戏设计师、结合 VR 的开放世界 AI，以及基于语音的 3D 打印。"],[257.28,261.13,46,"But it's still a course project, so it needs a research shape.","但这仍然是课程项目，所以需要有研究的形态。"],[261.48,267.88,46,"Two variants of your product, a metric you fix in advance, a cost table, and a short business memo.","产品的两个版本、一个事先固定的指标、一张成本表，以及一份简短的商业备忘录。"],[268.23,275.14,46,"And under Start from, you'll see two examples from our own campus, which I'll show you in a moment.","在“Start from”下面，你会看到两个来自我们校园的例子，我马上就会展示。"],[276.39,281.9,47,"If you choose Track H, here are the startup basics every team should be able to explain.","如果你选择 H 方向，这些是每个团队都应该能讲清楚的创业基础。"],[282.25,290.78,47,"Problem before product: interview about ten potential users about what they actually did in the past, not whether they like your idea.","先有问题，再有产品：访谈大约十位潜在用户，问他们过去实际做了什么，而不是问他们喜不喜欢你的点子。"],[291.13,295.36,47,"That's the Mom Test, because people are polite about ideas.","这就是 Mom Test，因为人们对别人的点子总是很客气。"],[295.71,301.16,47,"Write a Lean Canvas in week one, and again in week four, and show what changed.","在第一周写一份 Lean Canvas，第四周再写一份，并展示有哪些变化。"],[301.51,303.71,47,"Know your unit economics.","要清楚你的单位经济模型。"],[304.06,310.83,47,"Cost per active user per month is tokens times price, plus hosting, plus human review.","每位活跃用户每月的成本，等于 token 数乘以单价，加上托管费用，再加上人工审核。"],[311.18,316.35,47,"Compare that against what each user pays, and what it costs to acquire them.","再把它和每个用户支付的金额，以及获取一个用户的成本作比较。"],[316.7,322.18,47,"Ask the wrapper question: if the model vendor ships your feature tomorrow, what's left?","问自己“套壳”问题：如果模型厂商明天就上线了你的功能，你还剩下什么？"],[322.53,326.98,47,"Usually it's data, workflow, distribution or trust.","通常是数据、工作流、渠道或信任。"],[327.33,333.04,47,"For product-market fit, look for retention curves that flatten, and the Sean Ellis test.","关于产品与市场契合，要看留存曲线是否趋于平稳，以及 Sean Ellis 测试。"],[333.39,334.77,47,"Test one real price.","测试一个真实的价格。"],[335.12,341.83,47,"Check compliance, including China's two thousand twenty-three interim measures for generative AI services.","检查合规性，包括中国 2023 年的《生成式人工智能服务管理暂行办法》。"],[342.18,345.53,47,"And ship to twenty real users in week two.","并且在第二周就交付给 20 位真实用户。"],[346.78,354.62,48,"Here's a real example from our campus: FriesAI, or Shuta AI in Chinese, a student startup team that our group supports.","这是我们校园里的一个真实例子：薯塔AI，一个由我们课题组支持的学生创业团队。"],[354.97,360.75,48,"It's a study platform designed for Sino-foreign universities and international schools.","它是一个专为中外合作院校和国际学校设计的学习平台。"],[361.1,368.39,48,"Students share course slides, ask an AI questions about them, and search across documents for the concept they're stuck on.","学生可以分享课件，就课件内容向 AI 提问，还能跨文档检索自己卡住的知识点。"],[368.74,376.51,48,"According to the slide, it already has more than two thousand monthly active users, and serves most CUHK-Shenzhen courses.","根据幻灯片，它已经拥有超过两千名月活跃用户，覆盖港中深的大部分课程。"],[376.86,382.48,48,"And it is expanding to other joint-venture universities, and to universities abroad.","并且正在拓展到其他中外合办高校和国外高校。"],[382.83,391.44,48,"What I like about it: it started from the founders' own pain as students, trying to make sense of lecture slides before an exam.","我欣赏它的一点是：它源于创始人自己作为学生的痛点，考前努力看懂课件。"],[392.69,398.61,49,"And here are some numbers, as of April twelfth, two thousand twenty-five.","再看一些数据，截至 2025 年 4 月 12 日。"],[398.96,404.46,49,"Shuta AI covered about sixty percent of CUHK-Shenzhen undergraduates.","薯塔AI 已覆盖港中深约 60% 的本科生。"],[404.81,411.66,49,"There were three thousand five hundred seventy-nine registered users here, and four thousand six hundred eighty in total.","港中深注册人数达 3579 人，总注册人数达 4680 人。"],[412.01,418.4,49,"Daily active users were about twelve hundred, asking roughly twenty-nine hundred AI questions per day.","日活跃用户约 1200 人，平均每天提出约 2900 个 AI 问题。"],[418.75,422.59,49,"It was also being rolled out to seven other Sino-foreign universities.","它还在逐步推广到其他七所中外合办院校。"],[422.94,429.46,49,"Look at the screenshot: the interface is organised around real course codes and real lecture slides.","看这张截图：界面是围绕真实的课程代码和真实的课件组织的。"],[429.81,432.84,49,"That's what product-market fit looks like on a small scale.","这就是小规模的产品与市场契合。"],[433.19,438.55,49,"A specific group of users with a specific problem, who use it every day.","一群特定的用户，有一个特定的问题，并且每天都在使用。"],[439.8,442.35,50,"A second example, quite different.","第二个例子，风格完全不同。"],[442.7,446.23,50,"Our student Zhu Yuxuan combined tennis with AI.","我们的学生朱宇轩把网球和 AI 结合了起来。"],[446.58,454.73,50,"His app, called Wangshi, or TennSync in English, automatically cuts long tennis recordings into highlight clips.","他开发的 App 叫“网事”，英文名 TennSync，能自动把很长的网球录像剪成精彩集锦。"],[455.08,458.07,50,"So players don't have to scrub through hours of video.","这样球员就不用在几个小时的视频里来回拖进度条了。"],[458.42,465.4,50,"According to the slide, it has served over a thousand users, and saved tennis players more than five thousand hours.","根据幻灯片上的数据，它已服务一千多名用户，为网球爱好者节省了五千多个小时。"],[465.75,467.62,50,"He started from his own hobby.","他是从自己的爱好出发的。"],[467.97,475.14,50,"That's a pattern you'll see again and again: the best startup ideas often come from a problem you personally know very well.","这是一个你会反复看到的规律：最好的创业点子，往往来自你自己非常熟悉的问题。"]]},{"n":5,"title":"Fresh Ideas, Hospital Deployments and Picking a Topic","blurb":"Brainstorming ideas from robot bars to text-to-3D printing, agent deployments in the CUHK-Shenzhen hospital, and practical advice on choosing a topic and working with TAs.","file":"lecture08_part5.mp4","poster":"lecture08_part5.jpg","duration":713.8,"first":51,"last":68,"slides":[{"n":51,"title":"Some new ideas for brainstorming","t":0.8},{"n":52,"title":"Robot Bar","t":19.23},{"n":53,"title":"AI Seller","t":51.79},{"n":54,"title":"Expertise training","t":98.7},{"n":55,"title":"Open World Experience (using AI + VR Experience)","t":142.75},{"n":56,"title":"Text for 3D Printing","t":177.49},{"n":57,"title":"Text2Game/Text2APP","t":222.38},{"n":58,"title":"Startup Incubator simulator (创业孵化器的模拟器)","t":261.02},{"n":59,"title":"Special topic: applications in medicine (hospital deployment)","t":304.62},{"n":60,"title":"Medical Skills","t":357.46},{"n":61,"title":"OpenClaw 在港中深医院","t":397.65},{"n":62,"title":"OpenClaw 在港中深医院","t":436.19},{"n":63,"title":"Let me know if you are interested to deploy something in the CUHKSZ hospital. Email me via wangbenyou@cuhk.edu.cn","t":480.31},{"n":64,"title":"Triage","t":509.6},{"n":65,"title":"How to choose your topics","t":552.78},{"n":66,"title":"Relation between students and the teaching team","t":616.31},{"n":67,"title":"Relation between students and the teaching team","t":632.46},{"n":68,"title":"Discuss with your TAs","t":661.32}],"sents":[[0.8,4.92,51,"Beyond the eight tracks, I'd like to throw out a few new ideas for brainstorming.","在八个方向之外，我还想抛出几个新点子，供大家头脑风暴。"],[5.27,8.07,51,"These are not polished briefs; they're seeds.","它们不是打磨好的选题，而是一些种子。"],[8.42,10.69,51,"Some are playful, some are serious.","有的好玩，有的严肃。"],[11.04,17.83,51,"Treat them as prompts for your own thinking, and feel free to combine them with a track's methodology.","把它们当作启发自己思考的引子，也欢迎把它们和某个方向的方法论结合起来。"],[19.08,20.69,52,"First, a robot bar.","第一个，机器人酒吧。"],[21.04,26.2,52,"Picture a robot bartender that chats with you, remembers your usual drink, and mixes it.","想象一个机器人调酒师：它跟你聊天，记得你常点的酒，还能亲手调出来。"],[26.55,30.13,52,"It sounds playful, but it combines several hard problems.","听起来很好玩，但它融合了好几个难题。"],[30.48,38.06,52,"Spoken dialogue in a noisy room, memory of regular customers, and turning a conversation into precise physical actions.","嘈杂环境中的语音对话、对熟客的记忆，以及把一段对话转化为精确的物理动作。"],[38.41,42.03,52,"You can start in simulation, or with a simple robotic arm.","你可以从仿真开始，或者用一个简单的机械臂起步。"],[42.38,50.39,52,"A good project would measure something concrete, like order accuracy, or how many turns it takes to get the right drink.","好的项目会测量具体的东西，比如点单准确率，或者要几轮对话才能拿到对的那杯酒。"],[51.64,53.97,53,"Second, an AI seller.","第二个，AI 卖家。"],[54.32,58.37,53,"The diagram shows a full loop of AI-powered e-commerce.","这张图展示了一个完整的 AI 电商闭环。"],[58.72,65.46,53,"AI generates creative content like product videos, and it's promoted through Xiaohongshu-style posts.","AI 生成产品视频这类创意内容，再通过小红书式的帖子进行推广。"],[65.81,73.22,53,"Traffic is directed to Xianyu, the second-hand marketplace, where an AI handles the chat with buyers.","流量被引到二手交易平台闲鱼，由 AI 负责和买家聊天沟通。"],[73.57,75.46,53,"And then the item is shipped.","然后商品发货。"],[75.81,81.46,53,"That's brief H2 on the project page: an AI seller for a real small shop.","这就是项目页面上的选题 H2：为一家真实的小店打造 AI 卖家。"],[81.81,89.01,53,"The interesting questions are measurable: conversion rate, response time, and whether the AI describes products honestly.","有意思的问题都是可测量的：转化率、响应时间，以及 AI 描述商品是否诚实。"],[89.36,91.03,53,"That last one matters.","最后一点很重要。"],[91.38,97.3,53,"An AI seller that exaggerates would be an ethics problem, not a success.","一个夸大其词的 AI 卖家是伦理问题，而不是成功。"],[98.55,100.66,54,"Third, expertise training.","第三个，专业技能训练。"],[101.01,105.68,54,"On the left is a simulated patient for training medical students.","左边是一个用来训练医学生的模拟病人。"],[106.03,112.69,54,"The student talks to an AI patient by voice, takes a history, and has to arrive at a diagnosis.","学生通过语音和 AI 病人交谈、采集病史，最后要得出诊断。"],[113.04,116.96,54,"On the right is an AI interviewer for job-interview practice.","右边是一个用于求职面试练习的 AI 面试官。"],[117.31,124.27,54,"The appeal is obvious: real standardised patients and real interview coaches are expensive and hard to schedule.","它的吸引力显而易见：真实的标准化病人和面试教练都很贵，而且很难约时间。"],[124.62,127.91,54,"The research questions are about fidelity and transfer.","研究问题在于逼真度和迁移效果。"],[128.26,134.79,54,"Does the simulated patient behave like a real one, revealing information only when asked properly?","模拟病人的表现像真实病人吗？是不是只有问对了问题才会透露信息？"],[135.14,139.38,54,"And does practising with it actually improve performance with real people?","用它练习，真的能提高面对真人时的表现吗？"],[139.73,141.35,54,"This is brief H4.","这是选题 H4。"],[142.6,146.91,55,"Fourth, an open-world experience using AI and VR.","第四个，用 AI 加 VR 打造的开放世界体验。"],[147.26,151.35,55,"Imagine putting on a headset and walking into a fantasy world.","想象一下，戴上头显，走进一个奇幻世界。"],[151.7,160.76,55,"Every character, an elf, a robot guide, can actually talk with you, and react to what you say, instead of reading from a fixed script.","每个角色，不管是精灵还是机器人向导，都能真正和你对话、对你说的话做出反应，而不是照着固定剧本念。"],[161.11,167.35,55,"Brief H6 asks for an open-world AI and VR experience that people would actually pay for.","选题 H6 要求做一个人们真正愿意付费的开放世界 AI 加 VR 体验。"],[167.7,169.92,55,"That's a nice, honest constraint.","这是一个很好、很实在的约束。"],[170.27,176.09,55,"It forces you to find out what makes the experience valuable, rather than just technically impressive.","它逼着你去弄清楚，是什么让这个体验有价值，而不只是技术上炫酷。"],[177.34,179.75,56,"Fifth, text for 3D printing.","第五个，文本驱动的 3D 打印。"],[180.1,181.53,56,"Look at the three steps.","看这三个步骤。"],[181.88,186.02,56,"A user says one sentence: make me a cute 3D cat model.","用户说一句话：帮我生成一个可爱的小猫 3D 模型。"],[186.37,191.35,56,"A large model generates a 3D model file, like an STL or an OBJ.","大模型生成一个 3D 模型文件，比如 STL 或 OBJ。"],[191.7,195.57,56,"And the 3D printer prints it directly.","然后 3D 打印机直接把它打印出来。"],[195.92,197.88,56,"The tricky part is the middle step.","难点在中间这一步。"],[198.23,201.34,56,"A model that looks right on screen may not be printable.","一个在屏幕上看起来没问题的模型，未必能打印。"],[201.69,206.2,56,"It needs to be watertight, stable, and have parts that won't collapse.","它必须是封闭的、稳定的，各个部件也不能塌掉。"],[206.55,213.8,56,"Our lab's BlenderLLM, from a few slides ago, and work like Text2CAD are good starting points.","我们实验室几页前提到的 BlenderLLM，以及 Text2CAD 这类工作，都是很好的起点。"],[214.15,220.98,56,"Add speech input, and you get brief H7, speech-based 3D printing.","再加上语音输入，就是选题 H7：基于语音的 3D 打印。"],[222.23,225.17,57,"Sixth, text-to-game and text-to-app.","第六个，文本生成游戏和文本生成应用。"],[225.52,230.54,57,"A user says, I want a dinosaur city-builder game, and gets a playable game.","用户说“我想要一个恐龙城市建造游戏”，就能得到一个可以玩的游戏。"],[230.89,234.55,57,"Or describes an app, and gets a working one.","或者描述一个应用，就得到一个能用的应用。"],[234.9,238.23,57,"With today's coding agents, this is suddenly realistic.","有了今天的编程智能体，这件事一下子变得现实了。"],[238.58,243.3,57,"But the research question is about quality and evaluation.","但研究问题在于质量和评估。"],[243.65,247.67,57,"Does the generated game actually run? Is it playable? Is it fun?","生成的游戏真的能运行吗？能玩吗？好玩吗？"],[248.02,253.29,57,"That connects to Track A, where our lab's GameCraft-Bench evaluates exactly this.","这和方向 A 相关，我们实验室的 GameCraft-Bench 评估的正是这一点。"],[253.64,259.62,57,"And to brief H5, the AI game designer, if you want to put it in front of real users.","如果你想把它交给真实用户，那就对应选题 H5：AI 游戏设计师。"],[260.87,264.23,58,"Last idea: a startup incubator simulator.","最后一个点子：创业孵化器模拟器。"],[264.58,269.95,58,"The picture shows a simulated incubator, with a user pool and a VC zone.","图里是一个模拟的孵化器，有用户池，也有风投区。"],[270.3,275.97,58,"You put your app idea in, simulated users try it, and simulated investors judge it.","你把应用的点子放进去，模拟用户来试用，模拟投资人来评判。"],[276.32,281.67,58,"Then you iterate on your business model, before spending money in the real world.","然后在真实世界花钱之前，先迭代你的商业模式。"],[282.02,284.85,58,"This is a multi-agent simulation problem.","这是一个多智能体模拟问题。"],[285.2,291.02,58,"The key question, which you must answer honestly, is how well simulated users predict real ones.","关键问题是：模拟用户能多好地预测真实用户？这个问题你必须诚实回答。"],[291.37,297.13,58,"You'll see a past project, ConsumerSim, that did something similar for economic behaviour.","稍后你会看到往届的一个项目 ConsumerSim，它在经济行为上做了类似的事。"],[297.48,303.22,58,"If you try this, compare your simulation against at least some real user data.","如果你做这个题目，至少要拿一部分真实用户数据来和你的模拟做对比。"],[304.47,312.03,59,"Now a special topic close to my heart: medical applications, specifically deployment in a real hospital.","接下来是一个我特别关心的专题：医疗应用，具体来说是在真实医院里的部署。"],[312.38,314.47,59,"Here are the possible directions.","这里列出了几个可能的方向。"],[314.82,317.41,59,"First, an LLM for triage.","第一，用大模型做预分诊。"],[317.76,325.3,59,"It helps decide which department a patient should see and how urgent the case is, so staff can focus on the critical ones first.","它帮助判断病人该去哪个科室、病情有多紧急，让医护人员先集中处理危重病例。"],[325.65,330.29,59,"Then AI-assisted diagnosis, and X-ray report generation.","然后是 AI 辅助诊断，以及 X 光报告生成。"],[330.64,335.87,59,"Out-of-hospital management for diabetes patients, where most of the care happens at home.","糖尿病患者的院外管理，大部分照护其实发生在家里。"],[336.22,337.38,59,"Dental diagnosis.","牙科诊断。"],[337.73,340.66,59,"And OpenClaw agents running in hospitals.","还有在医院里运行的 OpenClaw 智能体。"],[341.01,344.8,59,"What makes medicine special is that errors have real consequences.","医疗的特殊之处在于，错误会带来真实的后果。"],[345.15,349.75,59,"So evaluation and safety matter even more than usual.","所以评估和安全比平时更加重要。"],[350.1,356.06,59,"We'll go much deeper into this next lecture, which is all about medical LLMs.","下一讲我们会深入讨论这个话题，那一讲专门讲医疗大模型。"],[357.31,360.93,60,"Here's one concrete resource: OpenClaw Medical Skills.","这里有一个具体的资源：OpenClaw Medical Skills。"],[361.28,369.04,60,"OpenClaw is the open-source agent framework, and this repository collects a large library of medical skills for it.","OpenClaw 是一个开源智能体框架，这个仓库为它收集了一个庞大的医疗技能库。"],[369.39,379.49,60,"The README lists eight hundred sixty-nine curated skills, covering clinical work, genomics, drug discovery, bioinformatics and medical devices.","README 里列出了 869 个精选技能，涵盖临床、基因组学、药物发现、生物信息学和医疗器械。"],[379.84,384.45,60,"It connects two ideas from today: skills from Track A, and medicine.","它把今天的两个主题连了起来：方向 A 里的技能，以及医疗。"],[384.8,389.85,60,"A project could add a new, well-tested skill for a specific clinical workflow.","一个项目可以为某个具体的临床流程新增一个经过充分测试的技能。"],[390.2,396.25,60,"Or it could evaluate how reliable the existing skills really are, on realistic cases.","也可以在真实病例上评估现有技能到底有多可靠。"],[397.5,403.25,61,"And this is it in action: OpenClaw at the CUHK-Shenzhen hospital.","这是它的实际应用：OpenClaw 在港中深医院。"],[403.6,409.52,61,"On the left, you can see a doctor's workstation, with the system on screen during a consultation.","左边可以看到医生的工作台，问诊时屏幕上运行着这个系统。"],[409.87,414.09,61,"On the right is the small NVIDIA machine it runs on.","右边是它所运行的那台小型 NVIDIA 主机。"],[414.44,417.5,61,"Notice that the hardware sits right there in the hospital.","注意，这台硬件就放在医院里。"],[417.85,424.88,61,"Running models locally keeps patient data on site, which is often a hard requirement in medicine.","在本地运行模型能让病人数据留在院内，这在医疗领域往往是硬性要求。"],[425.23,429.23,61,"It's a nice reminder that deployment isn't only about model accuracy.","这很好地提醒我们：部署不只关乎模型准确率。"],[429.58,434.79,61,"Privacy, cost, and fitting into the doctor's routine matter just as much.","隐私、成本，以及能否融入医生的日常工作流程，同样重要。"],[436.04,443.4,62,"Here's the interface: an intelligent medical-record assistant at the CUHK-Shenzhen hospital, called OpenClaw-Med.","这是它的界面：港中深医院的智能病历辅助系统，叫 OpenClaw-Med。"],[443.75,451.05,62,"On the left is the medical record form the doctor fills in: basic information, chief complaint, history.","左边是医生填写的病历表单：基本信息、主诉、病史。"],[451.4,455.11,62,"On the right, the agent works in two stages.","右边，智能体分两个阶段工作。"],[455.46,459.05,62,"Stage one generates a basic reference from the record.","第一阶段根据病历生成基本参考。"],[459.4,466.28,62,"Stage two, after the doctor adds examination results, generates suggestions for diagnosis and treatment.","第二阶段在医生补充检查结果之后，生成诊断和处置建议。"],[466.63,473.4,62,"Notice the design: the doctor stays in control at every step, and the AI only suggests.","注意这个设计：每一步都由医生掌控，AI 只提供建议。"],[473.75,478.91,62,"That human-in-the-loop design is what makes it acceptable in a real hospital.","正是这种人在回路中的设计，让它能在真实医院里被接受。"],[480.16,482.44,63,"So, an open invitation.","所以，这是一个公开邀请。"],[482.79,488.0,63,"If you're interested in deploying something in the CUHK-Shenzhen hospital, email me.","如果你有兴趣在港中深医院部署点什么，请给我发邮件。"],[488.35,490.5,63,"My address is right here on the slide.","我的邮箱地址就在幻灯片上。"],[490.85,493.94,63,"I'll be honest: real deployment takes time.","坦白说：真实部署需要时间。"],[494.29,498.82,63,"Patient data has strict rules, and anything that touches patients needs approval.","病人数据有严格的规定，任何涉及病人的事情都需要审批。"],[499.17,504.17,63,"So if this excites you, reach out early, this week rather than in December.","所以如果你对此感兴趣，请尽早联系，最好是这周，而不是等到十二月。"],[504.52,508.2,63,"And we'll figure out what's realistic within the course timeline.","我们会一起看看在课程时间内什么是现实可行的。"],[509.45,514.98,64,"One more medical example: triage, or more precisely, outpatient referral.","再举一个医疗的例子：分诊，更准确地说，是门诊导诊。"],[515.33,519.09,64,"When a patient arrives, which department should they go to?","病人来了，应该去哪个科室？"],[519.44,528.0,64,"Our paper here, Large Language Models for Outpatient Referral, defines the problem, builds a benchmark, and discusses the open challenges.","我们的这篇论文 Large Language Models for Outpatient Referral 定义了这个问题，构建了评测基准，并讨论了尚待解决的挑战。"],[528.35,536.11,64,"The screenshot shows a local health-service WeChat account in Longgang, with an AI-assisted appointment entry.","截图是龙岗当地的一个健康服务微信公众号，里面有一个 AI 辅助预约的入口。"],[536.46,540.54,64,"So this isn't just a research problem; it's a real service people use.","所以这不只是一个研究问题，而是人们真正在用的服务。"],[540.89,542.91,64,"It's a good model for a project.","这是一个很好的项目范式。"],[543.26,551.38,64,"Take a real workflow, define the task precisely, build an evaluation set, and then see how far current models get.","选一个真实的工作流程，精确地定义任务，构建评测集，然后看看现有模型能做到什么程度。"],[552.63,558.34,65,"After all those tracks and ideas, how do you actually choose? Here are three suggestions.","看了这么多方向和点子，到底该怎么选？这里有三条建议。"],[558.69,561.66,65,"First, combine your own expertise with AI.","第一，把你自己的专长和 AI 结合起来。"],[562.01,568.19,65,"If your previous major was math, physics or engineering, AI for your field might be the perfect project.","如果你之前的专业是数学、物理或工程，那么面向你所在领域的 AI，可能就是最合适的项目。"],[568.54,571.25,65,"You can judge the outputs better than most of us can.","因为你比我们大多数人都更能判断输出的好坏。"],[571.6,573.68,65,"Second, use your background.","第二，利用你的背景。"],[574.03,583.76,65,"If you come from a country or province whose language or dialect is under-represented in today's models, train or adapt an LLM for it.","如果你来自的国家或省份，其语言或方言在当今模型中代表性不足，那就为它训练或适配一个大模型。"],[584.11,592.91,65,"Or work on local culture: Huangmei opera, oracle bone script, Peking opera, traditional Chinese medicine, crosstalk.","或者做地方文化：黄梅戏、甲骨文、京剧、中医、相声。"],[593.26,596.26,65,"Third, look at the real needs of the people around you.","第三，关注你身边人的真实需求。"],[596.61,601.14,65,"Maybe a relative has diabetes and needs help managing it at home.","也许有位亲戚患有糖尿病，需要在家里管理病情。"],[601.49,605.61,65,"Or a friend has data or an application you could build on.","或者有朋友手里有数据或应用，你可以在此基础上开展工作。"],[605.96,610.31,65,"But the last line is the most important: your personal interest matters most.","但最后一行最重要：你的个人兴趣最重要。"],[610.66,614.91,65,"Four weeks is long when you're bored, and short when you're excited.","当你觉得无聊时，四周很漫长；当你充满热情时，四周转瞬即逝。"],[616.16,622.47,66,"Before we move on, let me ask: how do you see the relationship between you and the teaching team?","在继续之前，我想问一下：你如何看待你和教学团队之间的关系？"],[622.82,627.37,66,"Many students see it like this: we are the judges, and you are being judged.","很多同学是这样看的：我们是评委，你们是被评判的人。"],[627.72,631.06,66,"We grade you, and you try to impress us.","我们给你打分，你努力给我们留下好印象。"],[632.31,633.42,67,"Let me fix that.","让我来纠正一下。"],[633.77,636.0,67,"Cross out judge, and write help.","把“评判”划掉，写上“帮助”。"],[636.35,641.92,67,"Yes, we grade the projects in the end, but for the next five weeks, our job is to help you succeed.","没错，最后是我们给项目打分，但在接下来的五周里，我们的工作是帮助你们成功。"],[642.27,644.62,67,"So please, email the TAs and me.","所以，请给助教和我发邮件。"],[644.97,652.51,67,"Come to office hours with half-formed ideas, show us a failed experiment, or ask whether your evaluation is fair.","带着还没成形的想法来答疑时间，给我们看看失败的实验，或者问问你的评估是否公平。"],[652.86,654.01,67,"Make friends with them.","和他们交朋友。"],[654.36,659.92,67,"The teams that talk to us early almost always do better than the teams we only meet at the poster session.","早早来找我们交流的团队，几乎总是比那些到海报展示时才第一次见面的团队做得更好。"],[661.17,662.47,68,"Here are your TAs.","这是你们的助教。"],[662.82,665.13,68,"Look at the labels under their photos.","看看他们照片下面的标签。"],[665.48,674.16,68,"Between them, they've worked or interned at places like Microsoft, Qwen, Tencent, Kimi, MiniMax and Huawei.","他们在微软、Qwen、腾讯、Kimi、MiniMax 和华为等地方工作或实习过。"],[674.51,676.72,68,"And one has top VC experience.","还有一位有顶级风投的经历。"],[677.07,685.92,68,"So beyond your project, they're great people to ask about research careers, industry jobs, or how investors think about AI startups.","所以除了项目本身，你还可以向他们请教科研道路、业界工作，或者投资人怎么看 AI 创业。"],[686.27,688.53,68,"That's especially useful for Track H.","这对方向 H 尤其有用。"],[688.88,691.76,68,"Office hours for everyone are listed here.","每个人的答疑时间都列在这里。"],[692.11,697.77,68,"The TAs' emails and research directions are in the Teaching team section of the course homepage.","助教的邮箱和研究方向，在课程主页的教学团队栏目里。"],[698.12,700.44,68,"My own office hour is Friday evening.","我自己的答疑时间是周五晚上。"],[700.79,705.2,68,"Pick the TA whose background fits your topic, and go with a concrete question.","挑一位背景和你的题目相符的助教，带着具体的问题去找他。"],[705.55,711.94,68,"That wraps up topic selection. Next, let's see what strong projects actually look like.","选题部分就到这里。接下来，我们看看优秀的项目究竟是什么样子。"]]},{"n":6,"title":"Outstanding Projects from Past Terms","blurb":"What makes a project strong, the linked arXiv, GitHub and Hugging Face package, and past student projects from consumer simulation and trip planning to safety audits.","file":"lecture08_part6.mp4","poster":"lecture08_part6.jpg","duration":538.1,"first":69,"last":79,"slides":[{"n":69,"title":"Part3. Some Outstanding Projects","t":0.8},{"n":70,"title":"Some Outstanding Projects","t":17.51},{"n":71,"title":"Example: ArXiv+HF+Github","t":68.06},{"n":72,"title":"Slide 72","t":116.99},{"n":73,"title":"Slide 73","t":174.51},{"n":74,"title":"Slide 74","t":232.69},{"n":75,"title":"Slide 75","t":287.14},{"n":76,"title":"Slide 76","t":341.73},{"n":77,"title":"Slide 77","t":387.67},{"n":78,"title":"Slide 78","t":430.41},{"n":79,"title":"Slide 79","t":481.55}],"sents":[[0.8,3.82,69,"You know the rules, and you have plenty of ideas.","规则你们已经了解，点子也有很多了。"],[4.17,8.23,69,"The natural question now is: what does a really good project look like?","接下来自然的问题是：一个真正好的项目长什么样？"],[8.58,16.11,69,"Let's look at criteria first, then at several outstanding projects from past terms, both papers and posters.","我们先看评价标准，再看往届的几个优秀项目，包括论文和海报。"],[17.36,21.23,70,"First, what makes a good paper or project in general?","首先，一般来说，什么样的论文或项目才算好？"],[21.58,26.67,70,"The list is long, but it boils down to three things that map directly onto our grading.","这个清单很长，但归根结底是三件事，并且直接对应我们的评分标准。"],[27.02,30.23,70,"A valuable topic and real innovation.","有价值的选题和真正的创新。"],[30.58,36.86,70,"You're addressing an actual problem or filling a gap, with a perspective that's at least a little new.","你在解决一个真实的问题或填补一个空白，而且视角至少有一点新意。"],[37.21,44.56,70,"Solid evidence: thorough data analysis, and conclusions that follow from the data, not from hope.","扎实的证据：透彻的数据分析，以及从数据而不是从愿望中得出的结论。"],[44.91,52.03,70,"And clear communication: standard academic writing, a logical structure, and accurate citations.","还有清晰的表达：规范的学术写作、有逻辑的结构，以及准确的引用。"],[52.38,57.08,70,"Plus figures that are clear, labelled, and actually support the argument.","再加上清晰、标注完整、真正支撑论点的图表。"],[57.43,60.91,70,"Keep this list in mind as we go through the examples.","我们看例子的时候，请把这个清单记在心里。"],[61.26,66.66,70,"For each one, ask yourself which of these qualities makes it stand out.","每看一个，都问问自己：是哪些特质让它脱颖而出。"],[67.91,74.32,71,"First, an example of the complete package: arXiv plus Hugging Face plus GitHub.","先看一个“全套”的例子：arXiv 加 Hugging Face 加 GitHub。"],[74.67,78.9,71,"This is MedGen from our lab, about medical video generation.","这是我们实验室的 MedGen，做的是医学视频生成。"],[79.25,80.52,71,"Look at three things.","注意三件事。"],[80.87,83.12,71,"The paper is on arXiv.","论文发布在 arXiv 上。"],[83.47,88.49,71,"Right under the author list there's a GitHub link, so readers find the code immediately.","作者列表下面就有 GitHub 链接，读者能马上找到代码。"],[88.84,92.34,71,"The arrow on the slide says it: link your code here.","幻灯片上的箭头写得很清楚：在这里放上你的代码链接。"],[92.69,98.19,71,"And the GitHub page links to the paper, the dataset on Hugging Face, and the model.","而 GitHub 页面又链接到论文、Hugging Face 上的数据集，以及模型。"],[98.54,100.7,71,"Everything points to everything else.","所有东西都互相指向彼此。"],[101.05,104.21,71,"You don't have to post your project on arXiv.","你不一定要把项目发到 arXiv 上。"],[104.56,111.52,71,"But release your code and data in a clean, linked way, because it makes your work reproducible.","但请把代码和数据整洁地发布出来并互相链接，因为这让你的工作可复现。"],[111.87,115.59,71,"And remember, there's a bonus point for code reproducibility.","别忘了，代码可复现还有加分。"],[116.84,119.13,72,"Now some projects from past students.","接下来看几个往届同学的项目。"],[119.48,124.87,72,"This one is ConsumerSim, an LLM-based simulation of consumer behaviour.","这个是 ConsumerSim，一个基于大模型的消费者行为模拟系统。"],[125.22,131.48,72,"The question comes from economics: traditional models assume people are rational, but real people aren't.","问题来自经济学：传统模型假设人是理性的，但真实的人并不是。"],[131.83,136.38,72,"So they simulated hundreds of agents with different personas.","于是他们模拟了数百个具有不同人设的智能体。"],[136.73,138.89,72,"Each agent has a two-stage engine.","每个智能体都有一个两阶段引擎。"],[139.24,148.82,72,"First it perceives the news, and updates its mood and expectations; then it decides how to spend, with memory across periods.","先感知新闻，更新自己的情绪和预期；再决定如何消费，并且跨期保留记忆。"],[149.17,155.28,72,"What makes it good? A clear question from another field, and a clean architecture figure on the right.","它好在哪里？一个来自其他领域的清晰问题，以及右边这张清爽的架构图。"],[155.63,159.63,72,"And a quantitative result tied to economic theory.","还有一个与经济学理论挂钩的定量结果。"],[159.98,167.76,72,"They estimated how much of a durable-goods voucher people would actually spend, and checked it against known theories.","他们估计了人们实际会花掉多少耐用品消费券，并用已知理论做了验证。"],[168.11,173.11,72,"It's a nice example of the advice to combine your expertise with AI.","这是“把你的专长和 AI 结合”这条建议的一个好例子。"],[174.36,178.85,73,"Another past project: FutureSelf, an agent for career planning.","另一个往届项目：FutureSelf，一个用于职业规划的智能体。"],[179.2,187.47,73,"Students talk with AI-generated versions of their future selves, built with retrieval and a psychology framework called WOOP.","学生与 AI 生成的“未来的自己”对话，系统基于检索和一个叫 WOOP 的心理学框架构建。"],[187.82,192.07,73,"WOOP stands for wish, outcome, obstacle and plan.","WOOP 代表愿望、结果、障碍和计划。"],[192.42,196.48,73,"They ran a real user study with twenty-four participants.","他们做了一个真实的用户研究，有 24 名参与者。"],[196.83,202.79,73,"They compared talking to one focused future self with exploring several possible futures.","他们比较了两种方式：和一个聚焦的未来自我对话，以及探索多个可能的未来。"],[203.14,206.59,73,"Career goal clarity improved a lot in both conditions.","在两种条件下，职业目标清晰度都大幅提升。"],[206.94,211.95,73,"But, contrary to their hypothesis, exploring several futures was not better.","但和他们的假设相反，探索多个未来并没有更好。"],[212.3,218.45,73,"The interviews suggested it actually caused some decision anxiety. They called this the divergence paradox.","访谈表明，它反而带来了一些决策焦虑。他们把这称为“发散悖论”。"],[218.8,225.6,73,"That's what I love about this project: they reported a result that went against their own hypothesis, and explained it.","这正是我喜欢这个项目的地方：他们报告了一个与自己假设相悖的结果，并做出了解释。"],[225.95,231.29,73,"A well-explained negative result is worth more than an oversold positive one.","一个解释充分的负面结果，比一个被过度包装的正面结果更有价值。"],[232.54,237.12,74,"Next, TripGenie, an agent for planning trips across Chinese cities.","下一个是 TripGenie，一个为中国城市间旅行做规划的智能体。"],[237.47,238.88,74,"The problem is relatable.","这个问题大家都有共鸣。"],[239.23,246.1,74,"Planning a multi-city trip means juggling train schedules, hotel prices and attractions, under a budget.","规划多城市旅行，意味着要在预算内同时兼顾火车时刻、酒店价格和景点。"],[246.45,257.26,74,"TripGenie, built on DeepSeek-Chat, parses the user's constraints and calls three tools, for high-speed rail, attractions and hotels, across twenty-eight cities.","TripGenie 基于 DeepSeek-Chat，解析用户的约束，并调用高铁、景点和酒店三个工具，覆盖 28 个城市。"],[257.61,260.24,74,"Now look at the results in the abstract.","现在看看摘要里的结果。"],[260.59,267.31,74,"A final pass rate of eighteen point nine percent, versus sixteen percent for a greedy-search baseline.","最终通过率为 18.9%，而贪心搜索基线为 16%。"],[267.66,271.15,74,"That's not a huge number, and they say so openly.","这个数字并不大，他们也坦然承认了。"],[271.5,278.69,74,"They discuss the limits of current LLM planning and incomplete data, alongside feedback from twenty users.","他们讨论了当前大模型规划能力的局限和数据不完整的问题，同时给出了 20 位用户的反馈。"],[279.04,285.74,74,"An honest number with a proper baseline is far better than an impressive number without one.","一个有合适基线的诚实数字，远胜于一个没有基线的漂亮数字。"],[286.99,291.29,75,"And here's TripGenie's main figure, which is a good lesson in itself.","这是 TripGenie 的主图，它本身就是很好的一课。"],[291.64,296.53,75,"At the top left, a user asks for a three-day trip from Beijing to Shanghai with friends.","左上角，用户请求和朋友一起从北京去上海玩三天。"],[296.88,301.98,75,"The budget is about five thousand yuan, and they want at least a four-star hotel.","预算大约五千元，并且至少要四星级酒店。"],[302.33,308.05,75,"The agent analyses the constraints, and calls the train, hotel and attraction tools.","智能体分析这些约束，并调用火车、酒店和景点工具。"],[308.4,316.16,75,"It outputs a day-by-day plan with costs, a total of four thousand six hundred seventy yuan, with all constraints satisfied.","它输出一份带费用的逐日行程，总计四千六百七十元，所有约束全部满足。"],[316.51,320.57,75,"At the bottom left, they show the prompting strategies they compared.","左下角展示了他们比较过的各种提示策略。"],[320.92,328.33,75,"Direct prompting, zero-shot chain-of-thought, tree of thoughts, ReAct, Reflexion and greedy search.","直接提示、零样本思维链、思维树、ReAct、Reflexion，以及贪心搜索。"],[328.68,334.66,75,"One figure tells the whole story: input, method, compared alternatives, and output.","一张图讲完整个故事：输入、方法、对比方案和输出。"],[335.01,340.33,75,"If someone only looks at this figure, they understand the project. Aim for that.","就算只看这一张图，也能理解整个项目。请以此为目标。"],[341.58,346.88,76,"Now some past posters. This one is Safety Evaluation of Local LLMs.","接下来看几张往届的海报。这张是“本地大模型的安全性评估”。"],[347.23,351.7,76,"The team deployed five open models locally using Ollama.","团队用 Ollama 在本地部署了五个开源模型。"],[352.05,361.36,76,"They tested them with the Do-Not-Answer dataset, which contains prompts a responsible model should refuse, organised by risk area and harm type.","他们用 Do-Not-Answer 数据集来测试，其中的提示是负责任的模型应当拒绝的，并按风险领域和危害类型组织。"],[361.71,369.44,76,"They scored responses automatically with a fine-tuned Longformer classifier, and added human evaluation for deeper insight.","他们用微调过的 Longformer 分类器自动给回答打分，并加入人工评估以获得更深入的洞察。"],[369.79,372.13,76,"What's good here is the evaluation protocol.","这里的亮点是评估方案。"],[372.48,377.72,76,"A public dataset, an automatic scorer, plus human checks of that scorer.","公开数据集、自动评分器，再加上对评分器的人工核查。"],[378.07,380.93,76,"Notice they didn't train any big model at all.","注意，他们根本没有训练任何大模型。"],[381.28,386.27,76,"A careful evaluation of existing models is a complete, respectable project.","对现有模型做一次认真细致的评估，本身就是一个完整、体面的项目。"],[387.52,392.25,77,"This poster is about multi-agent cooperation for writing internet novels.","这张海报讲的是用多智能体协作来写网络小说。"],[392.6,398.23,77,"Several agents take different roles: outline, beginning, body content and memory.","多个智能体分担不同角色：大纲、开头、正文和记忆。"],[398.58,403.27,77,"And an external vector store keeps the story consistent across chapters.","外部向量库则保证故事在各章节之间保持一致。"],[403.62,409.84,77,"It's a nice, clear system design, and the methodology block shows the architecture well.","这是一个清晰漂亮的系统设计，方法部分把架构展示得很好。"],[410.19,415.93,77,"One thing I'd push them on: the results use GPT-4 to score text consistency.","有一点我会追问他们：结果部分用 GPT-4 来给文本一致性打分。"],[416.28,420.52,77,"Remember the rule of thumb from the project page: use an independent checker.","记住项目页面上的经验法则：使用独立的检验方。"],[420.87,429.01,77,"When an LLM judges LLM output, check that judge against some human ratings, at least on a sample.","当用大模型评判大模型的输出时，至少要在一个样本上，用人工评分来检验这个评判者。"],[430.26,435.87,78,"StockGPT, which we saw earlier on the requirements slide. Here's the full poster.","StockGPT，我们之前在要求那页见过。这是完整的海报。"],[436.22,438.22,78,"It's a two-stage method.","这是一个两阶段的方法。"],[438.57,443.83,78,"First, they fine-tune Qwen to extract sentiment from financial news and reports.","第一阶段，他们微调 Qwen，从财经新闻和报告中提取情感。"],[444.18,453.51,78,"Second, they use the fine-tuned model's embeddings of research reports as features for an XGBoost model that recommends stocks.","第二阶段，用微调后模型对研报的嵌入作为特征，输入一个推荐股票的 XGBoost 模型。"],[453.86,460.75,78,"Then they backtest it on the A-share market, against the CSI five hundred index.","然后在 A 股市场上做回测，以中证 500 指数为基准。"],[461.1,463.25,78,"Look at how well organised the poster is.","看看这张海报组织得多好。"],[463.6,474.07,78,"Introduction, motivation with a word cloud of financial reports, a clear two-stage method diagram, data details, and backtest results with charts.","引言、配有财报词云的动机、清晰的两阶段方法图、数据细节，以及带图表的回测结果。"],[474.42,480.15,78,"A reader can follow it top to bottom in a minute. That's what a well-presented poster looks like.","读者一分钟就能从上读到下。这就是一张展示得好的海报该有的样子。"],[481.4,485.34,79,"Last poster: In-context learning, LLM conversion.","最后一张海报：上下文学习与大模型转换。"],[485.69,491.32,79,"This one is different, because it's an analysis project rather than a system.","这一张不太一样，因为它是一个分析型项目，而不是一个系统。"],[491.67,496.08,79,"The team asked how LLMs actually learn from the examples in a prompt.","团队研究的问题是：大模型究竟如何从提示中的示例里学习。"],[496.43,502.31,79,"They used saliency scores that track how information flows between tokens across layers.","他们使用显著性分数，追踪信息在各层中如何在词元之间流动。"],[502.66,507.49,79,"And they tested two hypotheses on several tasks, including code.","并在包括代码在内的多个任务上检验了两个假设。"],[507.84,513.54,79,"In shallow layers, information gathers into the label words of the demonstrations.","在浅层，信息汇聚到示例的标签词上。"],[513.89,520.4,79,"In deeper layers, the model uses those label words as anchors for its final prediction.","在深层，模型把这些标签词当作锚点来做最终预测。"],[520.75,525.31,79,"Essentially, they re-tested a published finding on new kinds of tasks.","本质上，他们是在新类型的任务上重新检验了一个已发表的发现。"],[525.66,528.42,79,"The lesson: you don't have to build a product.","启示是：你不一定要做一个产品。"],[528.77,536.27,79,"Reproducing and stress-testing a known result in new settings is solid science, and very feasible in four weeks.","在新场景中复现并压力测试一个已知结论，是扎实的科学工作，而且四周内完全可行。"]]},{"n":7,"title":"Writing Your Paper: Tips That Save Points","blurb":"From abstract to concrete, less is more, motivating every component, defining terms, clear logic and consistent style: the writing habits behind 15 percent of the grade, then a wrap-up.","file":"lecture08_part7.mp4","poster":"lecture08_part7.jpg","duration":804.8,"first":80,"last":98,"slides":[{"n":80,"title":"Part4. Paper Writing","t":0.8},{"n":81,"title":"https://sakana.ai/ai-scientist-first-publication/","t":22.78},{"n":82,"title":"Writing tips, poster and paper samples: one page","t":75.21},{"n":83,"title":"Tips of NLP report writing","t":120.12},{"n":84,"title":"From abstract to concrete","t":149.16},{"n":85,"title":"Example","t":188.84},{"n":86,"title":"Less is more","t":239.92},{"n":87,"title":"Motivation for the whole paper","t":282.31},{"n":88,"title":"Motivation for almost most components","t":321.2},{"n":89,"title":"Don’t try to sound smart","t":362.75},{"n":90,"title":"Be concise","t":391.57},{"n":91,"title":"Do not use a new term that was not explained","t":429.67},{"n":92,"title":"Be clear and specific","t":480.64},{"n":93,"title":"Use fluent logic","t":529.17},{"n":94,"title":"Consistent style","t":571.51},{"n":95,"title":"Other tips","t":615.17},{"n":96,"title":"Q&A","t":662.99},{"n":97,"title":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=I44_zbEwz_w","t":732.77},{"n":98,"title":"Slide 98","t":764.26}],"sents":[[0.8,4.84,80,"Those were some of the strongest projects from past terms.","以上是往届最优秀的一些项目。"],[5.19,8.74,80,"What they all share, besides good ideas, is clear communication.","除了好的想法，它们的共同点是表达清晰。"],[9.09,15.15,80,"And remember, writing clarity alone is worth fifteen points, a third of your report grade.","别忘了，光是写作清晰度就占十五分，是报告成绩的三分之一。"],[15.5,21.38,80,"So let's finish with paper writing: the habits that make a paper easy and pleasant to read.","所以最后我们来讲论文写作：那些让论文易读、读起来舒服的习惯。"],[22.63,25.98,81,"Let me start with something a bit provocative.","我先说一件有点挑衅意味的事。"],[26.33,38.43,81,"In two thousand twenty-five, Sakana AI announced that a paper generated entirely by their system, The AI Scientist, passed peer review at an ICLR workshop.","2025 年，Sakana AI 宣布，一篇完全由他们的系统 The AI Scientist 生成的论文，通过了 ICLR 一个研讨会的同行评审。"],[38.78,47.13,81,"You can see the paper here: Compositional Regularization, Unexpected Obstacles in Enhancing Neural Network Generalization.","论文就在这里：《组合正则化：增强神经网络泛化时的意外障碍》。"],[47.48,50.47,81,"Interestingly, it reports a negative result.","有意思的是，它报告的是一个负面结果。"],[50.82,54.99,81,"So AI can now write a passable paper. What does that mean for you?","所以 AI 现在已经能写出一篇过得去的论文了。这对你们意味着什么？"],[55.34,60.26,81,"You're allowed to use AI tools in your project, but describe how you used them in your report.","你们可以在项目中使用 AI 工具，但要在报告里说明是如何使用的。"],[60.61,64.44,81,"And remember, you're responsible for every claim.","记住，你要为每一个论断负责。"],[64.79,71.2,81,"It also means the bar for human writing is clarity and real insight, not just fluent text.","这也意味着，对人类写作的要求是清晰和真正的洞见，而不只是文字流畅。"],[71.55,73.81,81,"That's what the next slides are about.","这正是接下来几页要讲的内容。"],[75.06,84.93,82,"All the writing tips I'm about to show, plus past posters and papers, are collected on one page on the course site: the writing-tips page linked here.","我接下来要讲的所有写作技巧，以及往届的海报和论文，都汇集在课程网站的一个页面上，就是这里链接的写作技巧页面。"],[85.28,89.79,82,"The short version: a good paper reads like a film with no dull stretch.","简而言之：一篇好论文读起来就像一部没有冷场的电影。"],[90.14,95.07,82,"Go from abstract to concrete, less is more, and motivate every component.","从抽象到具体，少即是多，并且为每个组件说明动机。"],[95.42,96.99,82,"Don't try to sound smart.","不要刻意显得聪明。"],[97.34,104.44,82,"Be concise, define every new term, be clear and specific, keep your logic fluent, and keep a consistent style.","要简洁，定义每一个新术语，清晰具体，逻辑流畅，风格一致。"],[104.79,106.94,82,"Related work is not a shopping list.","相关工作不是购物清单。"],[107.29,115.85,82,"And for the poster session, remember the four-minute pitch formula: your question, your comparison figure, one failure, one limitation.","海报展示时，记住四分钟陈述的公式：你的问题、你的对比图、一次失败、一个局限。"],[116.2,118.72,82,"Now let's go through these one by one.","下面我们逐条来看。"],[119.97,123.49,83,"Here's the one sentence I'd like you to remember, in Chinese.","这是我希望你们记住的一句话，用中文说。"],[123.84,127.84,83,"A good paper should read like a smooth movie, with no niao dian.","一篇好的论文读起来，应该像看一部流畅的电影，没有尿点。"],[128.19,134.91,83,"A niao dian is the moment in a film where you think: I can go to the bathroom now, I won't miss anything.","所谓尿点，就是看电影时你心想“现在去趟洗手间也不会错过什么”的那一刻。"],[135.26,136.83,83,"Your paper shouldn't have one.","你的论文不应该有这样的时刻。"],[137.18,142.84,83,"Every paragraph should either move the story forward, or give the reader something they need.","每一段要么推动故事向前，要么给读者提供他们需要的东西。"],[143.19,147.76,83,"If a section could be skipped without losing anything, either make it matter, or cut it.","如果某一节跳过也不损失什么，要么让它变得重要，要么删掉。"],[149.01,152.43,84,"First tip: go from abstract to concrete.","第一条：从抽象到具体。"],[152.78,155.62,84,"Give the general picture first, then the details.","先给出整体图景，再讲细节。"],[155.97,161.35,84,"Look at this bowl of snack mix: pretzels, crackers, cereal, all mixed together.","看这碗混合零食：椒盐卷饼、饼干、麦片，全都混在一起。"],[161.7,168.21,84,"That's what it feels like to read a paper that throws all the details at you before telling you what the method is for.","读一篇还没告诉你方法用来干什么、就把所有细节一股脑丢给你的论文，就是这种感觉。"],[168.56,174.32,84,"The reader holds each piece in their head without knowing where it fits, and that's exhausting.","读者把每一块都记在脑子里，却不知道它该放在哪，这非常累人。"],[174.67,180.56,84,"So start each section, and even each paragraph, with the big picture: what we're doing and why.","所以每一节，甚至每一段，都要先讲大图景：我们在做什么，为什么做。"],[180.91,182.74,84,"Then go into the details.","然后再深入细节。"],[183.09,187.44,84,"The reader then has a map, and every detail has a place to go.","这样读者手里就有了一张地图，每个细节都有地方安放。"],[188.69,199.05,85,"Here's a concrete example of that, from a paper by Ravi and colleagues in two thousand twenty-three, quoted in a nice blog post on writing NLP papers.","这里有一个具体例子，来自 Ravi 等人 2023 年的论文，被一篇关于 NLP 论文写作的好博客引用过。"],[199.4,201.39,85,"Read how the method section opens.","看看方法部分是怎么开头的。"],[201.74,203.99,85,"It points to the architecture figure.","它先指向架构图。"],[204.34,208.46,85,"It says what they reuse from prior work, and what they change.","它说明了沿用了前人工作的哪些部分，又改了什么。"],[208.81,216.46,85,"It states the goal: resolving coreferences where the two mentions aren't similar on the surface, but are linked by commonsense.","它点明目标：解决那些表面上不相似、但通过常识相关联的指称之间的共指问题。"],[216.81,225.32,85,"And then it says: so we build a commonsense inference engine in Section three point one, and use it to improve the scorer in Section three point two.","然后它说：因此我们在 3.1 节构建一个常识推理引擎，并在 3.2 节用它改进打分器。"],[225.67,231.52,85,"In four sentences, the reader knows the whole plan, and where to find each part.","短短四句话，读者就知道了整体计划，以及每部分在哪里。"],[231.87,238.52,85,"Steal this pattern: one overview paragraph at the top of each technical section, pointing to the subsections.","把这个模式学过去：在每个技术章节开头放一段概述，指向各个小节。"],[239.77,241.85,86,"Second tip: less is more.","第二条：少即是多。"],[242.2,243.32,86,"Look at this picture.","看这张图。"],[243.67,249.38,86,"The research path from A to B is a tangled mess of loops, dead ends and false starts.","从 A 到 B 的研究路径，是一团缠绕的乱麻，充满了绕圈、死胡同和走错的路。"],[249.73,252.87,86,"The paper path from A to B is a straight line.","而论文中从 A 到 B 的路径，是一条直线。"],[253.22,254.48,86,"That's how it should be.","本该如此。"],[254.83,259.53,86,"Your reader doesn't need the history of everything you tried, successful or not.","读者不需要知道你尝试过的所有东西的来龙去脉，不论成功与否。"],[259.88,265.76,86,"They need the most direct route to your main findings. Not every finding, just the main ones.","他们需要的是通往你主要发现的最直接路线。不是每个发现，只是主要的那些。"],[266.11,272.17,86,"This is hard emotionally, because you worked on those dead ends, and you want credit for them.","这在情感上很难，因为你在那些死胡同上花了功夫，也希望得到认可。"],[272.52,280.91,86,"But if a failed attempt teaches the reader something, put it briefly in the analysis or the appendix. Otherwise, let it go.","但如果某次失败的尝试能给读者带来启发，就在分析或附录里简要写一下；否则，就放下吧。"],[282.16,283.96,87,"Third tip: motivation.","第三条：动机。"],[284.31,286.76,87,"Your whole paper needs a clear motivation.","整篇论文需要一个清晰的动机。"],[287.11,292.25,87,"Why should anyone care about this problem, and why isn't it already solved?","为什么有人应该关心这个问题？为什么它还没有被解决？"],[292.6,298.88,87,"Students often jump straight into the method, because the method is what they spent their time on.","同学们常常直接跳进方法部分，因为方法是他们花时间最多的地方。"],[299.23,305.1,87,"But without motivation, the reader can't tell whether your method is clever or pointless.","但没有动机，读者就分辨不出你的方法是巧妙还是毫无意义。"],[305.45,313.23,87,"Sometimes I even ask my own students to write an independent section called Motivation, just to force themselves to articulate it.","有时我甚至让自己的学生单独写一节叫“动机”，就是为了逼他们把它讲清楚。"],[313.58,319.8,87,"You don't need a separate section in your report, but you need the content, usually in the introduction.","你的报告不需要单独一节，但需要有这部分内容，通常放在引言里。"],[321.05,326.06,88,"And motivation isn't only for the whole paper; almost every component needs one too.","动机不只是整篇论文需要，几乎每个组件也都需要。"],[326.41,330.71,88,"Here's an example from a paper on generating math questions.","这是一篇关于生成数学题的论文中的例子。"],[331.06,337.52,88,"They build three directed acyclic graphs: one over topics, one over knowledge points, and a hybrid one.","他们构建了三个有向无环图：一个基于主题，一个基于知识点，还有一个混合图。"],[337.87,341.25,88,"And they generate new questions by random walks over them.","并通过在图上随机游走来生成新题目。"],[341.6,348.32,88,"The callout asks the question every reviewer will ask: why not a simpler structure? Why is a DAG necessary?","批注框里问的正是每个审稿人都会问的：为什么不用更简单的结构？为什么必须用 DAG？"],[348.67,352.62,88,"If you introduce a component, answer that question in the text.","如果你引入一个组件，就要在正文里回答这个问题。"],[352.97,357.62,88,"Ideally, back it with an ablation that shows what happens without it.","最好再用消融实验支撑，展示去掉它会怎样。"],[357.97,361.35,88,"Every design choice should come with a because.","每一个设计选择，都应该有一个“因为”。"],[362.6,366.46,89,"Fourth tip, and a short one: don't try to sound smart.","第四条，很简短：不要刻意显得聪明。"],[366.81,369.71,89,"Utilize, or use? Just say use.","用 utilize 还是 use？直接说 use。"],[370.06,371.15,89,"It's perfectly fine.","完全没问题。"],[371.5,375.62,89,"Fancy words don't make your work look more serious; they make it harder to read.","花哨的词不会让你的工作显得更严肃，只会让它更难读。"],[375.97,382.03,89,"Especially for readers whose first language isn't English, which is most of the NLP community.","尤其是对母语不是英语的读者，而这正是 NLP 社区的大多数人。"],[382.38,385.67,89,"Write the simplest sentence that is still precise.","写出仍然精确的最简单的句子。"],[386.02,390.17,89,"Clever ideas in plain language are what impress reviewers.","用朴素的语言表达聪明的想法，才是打动审稿人的方式。"],[391.42,395.11,90,"Fifth: be concise. Look at the words crossed out.","第五条：简洁。看看被划掉的词。"],[395.46,398.78,90,"We evaluated our method on five distinct datasets.","“我们在五个不同的数据集上评估了我们的方法。”"],[399.13,403.38,90,"Distinct adds nothing; of course they're different datasets.","“不同的”这个词毫无信息量，它们当然是不同的数据集。"],[403.73,408.21,90,"If they really cover different kinds of data, show it in a table.","如果它们确实涵盖了不同类型的数据，就用一张表展示出来。"],[408.56,410.53,90,"We're proposing a novel method.","“我们提出了一种新颖的方法。”"],[410.88,415.29,90,"Of course it's new; you wouldn't propose an existing one.","当然是新的，你总不会提出一个已有的方法。"],[415.64,420.33,90,"And whether it's novel is for the reviewer to judge, not for you to announce.","而且是否新颖应该由审稿人来判断，而不是由你来宣布。"],[420.68,428.27,90,"When you edit, go through each sentence, and ask of every adjective: does this word add information? If not, delete it.","修改时，逐句检查，对每个形容词都问一句：这个词增加了信息吗？如果没有，删掉。"],[429.52,432.85,91,"Sixth: never use a new term without explaining it.","第六条：永远不要使用未经解释的新术语。"],[433.2,437.61,91,"Here's a real bad example from a draft by one of my PhD students.","这是我一位博士生草稿里的一个真实反例。"],[437.96,450.07,91,"Complementing our primary findings, we also delve into comprehensive ablation studies, uncovering several non-obvious insights pertinent to GPT-Instruct frameworks.","“作为主要发现的补充，我们还深入开展了全面的消融研究，揭示了与 GPT-Instruct 框架相关的若干非显而易见的洞见。”"],[450.42,456.39,91,"What is a GPT-Instruct framework? I'd never seen the term. Neither will your reader.","什么是 GPT-Instruct 框架？我从没见过这个术语，你的读者也不会见过。"],[456.74,464.42,91,"If you need a new term, define it clearly the first time it appears; otherwise, use the term everyone already knows.","如果你需要一个新术语，就在它第一次出现时清楚地定义；否则，就用大家都熟悉的术语。"],[464.77,473.45,91,"And while we're here, notice how delve into, comprehensive, and non-obvious insights sound impressive, but say very little.","顺便注意一下，“深入探究”“全面的”“非显而易见的洞见”这些词听起来很厉害，其实没说什么。"],[473.8,479.24,91,"That style often appears when writing is generated by a language model. Readers notice.","这种风格常常出现在语言模型生成的文字里。读者是能看出来的。"],[480.49,483.14,92,"Seventh: be clear and specific.","第七条：清晰而具体。"],[483.49,493.84,92,"Read this sentence: While these methodologies have proven effective, the exploration space is inherently confined to manually designed operations.","读一下这句话：“虽然这些方法已被证明有效，但探索空间本质上局限于人工设计的操作。”"],[494.19,499.26,92,"Exploration space of what? The reader has no idea what it refers to.","什么东西的探索空间？读者完全不知道它指的是什么。"],[499.61,508.41,92,"Every term should be grounded in something concrete: the space of questions? Of prompts? Of programs? Say which.","每个术语都应该落到具体的东西上：是题目的空间？提示的空间？还是程序的空间？要说清楚。"],[508.76,510.69,92,"The picture is a nice reminder.","这幅图是一个很好的提醒。"],[511.04,518.88,92,"In Chinese painting, liu bai, leaving blank space, invites the viewer to imagine, like that small boat on empty water.","在中国画里，“留白”给观者留下想象空间，就像空旷水面上的那叶小舟。"],[519.23,520.58,92,"That's beautiful in art.","这在艺术中很美。"],[520.93,527.77,92,"In scientific writing, though, blank space just means the reader has to guess, and different readers will guess differently.","但在科学写作中，留白只意味着读者得去猜，而不同的读者会猜出不同的意思。"],[529.02,534.95,93,"Eighth: use fluent logic. It's the same sentence again, but now look at the logic.","第八条：逻辑流畅。还是同一句话，但这次看它的逻辑。"],[535.3,540.62,93,"The sentence claims that manually designed operations hurt generalisation.","这句话声称，人工设计的操作会损害泛化能力。"],[540.97,545.35,93,"Why? The link is missing, so the reader has to invent it.","为什么？中间的环节缺失了，读者只能自己去脑补。"],[545.7,548.67,93,"The fix, at the bottom, spells out the chain.","底部的修改版把这条因果链完整写了出来。"],[549.02,553.47,93,"Manual design is too labour-intensive to cover a large range of questions.","人工设计太耗费人力，无法覆盖大量的题目。"],[553.82,557.54,93,"And that limited coverage is what hurts generalisation.","而正是这种有限的覆盖面损害了泛化能力。"],[557.89,560.94,93,"Each step now follows from the previous one.","现在每一步都由上一步自然推出。"],[561.29,570.11,93,"When you revise, look for every which leads to, or thus, in your draft, and check that the reasoning between the two halves is actually written down.","修改时，找出草稿里每一个“从而导致”或“因此”，检查前后两半之间的推理是否真的写了出来。"],[571.36,575.33,94,"Ninth: consistent style. Here's the same table twice.","第九条：风格一致。这是同一张表格的两个版本。"],[575.68,579.5,94,"The top one has lines everywhere, around every cell.","上面这张到处都是线，每个单元格都被框起来。"],[579.85,585.48,94,"The bottom one is a three-line table: one line at the top, one under the header, one at the bottom.","下面这张是三线表：顶部一条线，表头下一条线，底部一条线。"],[585.83,589.6,94,"Which is easier to read? The bottom one, clearly.","哪个更好读？显然是下面这张。"],[589.95,593.07,94,"The grid lines in the top one are just visual noise.","上面那张的网格线只是视觉噪音。"],[593.42,596.85,94,"In LaTeX, use the booktabs package to get this style.","在 LaTeX 中，用 booktabs 宏包就能得到这种样式。"],[597.2,607.34,94,"More generally, be consistent: the same number of decimal places, the same fonts and colours across figures, and the same name for the same thing throughout the paper.","更广泛地说，要保持一致：相同的小数位数，各图使用相同的字体和颜色，同一个东西在全文用同一个名字。"],[607.69,613.77,94,"Consistency makes the work look careful, and readers assume careful-looking work was done carefully.","一致性让工作看起来很严谨，而读者会认为看起来严谨的工作也是严谨地完成的。"],[615.02,616.39,95,"A few final tips.","最后几条建议。"],[616.74,623.09,95,"Make your paper self-contained: a reader shouldn't need to read three other papers to follow yours.","让你的论文自成一体：读者不应该需要先读另外三篇论文才能看懂你的。"],[623.44,626.58,95,"Don't repeat the same point within a section.","同一节里不要重复同一个观点。"],[626.93,632.1,95,"Avoid overly long sentences; if a sentence needs to be read twice, split it.","避免过长的句子；如果一句话需要读两遍，就把它拆开。"],[632.45,635.69,95,"Don't oversell. Be honest about limitations.","不要过度包装。诚实地面对局限。"],[636.04,641.63,95,"Reviewers, and TAs, trust a paper more when it clearly says what doesn't work.","当论文清楚地说明哪些地方行不通时，审稿人和助教会更信任它。"],[641.98,644.89,95,"And the related work section is not a shopping list.","还有，相关工作部分不是购物清单。"],[645.24,649.59,95,"Don't just write: A did this, B did that, C did something else.","不要只写：A 做了这个，B 做了那个，C 做了别的。"],[649.94,657.4,95,"Group the papers by theme, say what each group achieved and where it falls short, and use that to show the gap your work fills.","按主题把论文分组，说明每组取得了什么、不足在哪，再用它来凸显你的工作所填补的空白。"],[657.75,661.59,95,"Done well, related work is part of your motivation.","写得好的话，相关工作本身就是你动机的一部分。"],[662.84,663.85,96,"Let me wrap up.","我来总结一下。"],[664.2,670.5,96,"The final project is fifty-five percent of your grade: ten points for the poster, and forty-five for the report.","期末项目占总成绩的 55%：海报 10 分，报告 45 分。"],[670.85,681.18,96,"The poster presentation is on December eighteenth, and the poster file is due by five in the afternoon on December seventeenth, so we can print it.","海报展示在 12 月 18 日，海报文件须在 12 月 17 日下午五点前提交，方便我们打印。"],[681.53,686.86,96,"The report, at most six pages of main text, is due on December twenty-fifth.","报告正文最多六页，12 月 25 日截止。"],[687.21,694.1,96,"Teams of two or three are suggested, solo work is allowed, and every report carries a clear contribution statement.","建议两到三人组队，也允许单人完成，每份报告都要附上清晰的贡献说明。"],[694.45,702.01,96,"For your topic, choose one of the eight tracks on the project guide page, or propose your own LLM-related idea.","选题方面，可以从项目指南页面的八个方向中选一个，也可以提出你自己与大模型相关的想法。"],[702.36,710.92,96,"And follow the rule of thumb: one change, matched budget, held-out split, independent checker, seeds, and replayable traces.","并遵循经验法则：一个改动、预算匹配、留出测试集、独立检验、多个随机种子，以及可回放的轨迹。"],[711.27,713.35,96,"Pick something you genuinely care about.","选一个你真正在乎的题目。"],[713.7,718.6,96,"Talk to the TAs and to me early; we're here to help, not just to judge.","尽早和助教以及我交流；我们是来帮忙的，而不只是来评判的。"],[718.95,724.42,96,"And write clearly, because clarity is worth as many points as soundness.","还要写清楚，因为清晰度和技术严谨性的分值一样多。"],[724.77,731.37,96,"If you have questions about the final project, feel free to ask me, by email or in office hours.","如果你对期末项目有任何问题，欢迎通过邮件或在答疑时间来问我。"],[732.62,737.93,97,"Before we finish, here's a short video of a humanoid robot moving around in a lab.","结束之前，给大家看一段人形机器人在实验室里活动的短视频。"],[738.28,742.2,97,"I'm showing it as a reminder of how fast this field moves.","我放它是想提醒大家，这个领域发展得有多快。"],[742.55,746.05,97,"A few years ago, LLMs could only chat.","几年前，大模型还只会聊天。"],[746.4,752.43,97,"Now they write code, run as agents, and are starting to power robots that act in the physical world.","现在它们会写代码、作为智能体运行，还开始驱动在物理世界中行动的机器人。"],[752.78,762.86,97,"Several briefs in Track C, like embodied agents and robust vision-language-action policies, are small steps in that direction, and they're open to you.","方向 C 中的几个选题，比如具身智能体和鲁棒的视觉-语言-动作策略，都是朝这个方向迈出的小步，欢迎大家来做。"],[764.11,770.37,98,"And one last image: the Unitree G1 humanoid robot dancing alongside a person.","最后一张图：宇树 Unitree G1 人形机器人和一个人一起跳舞。"],[770.72,774.71,98,"With the slogan, sheng ming zai yu yun dong: life is about movement.","配的口号是“生命在于运动”。"],[775.06,779.31,98,"I'll take that literally as my closing message: get moving.","我就把它当作字面意思，作为今天的结束语：动起来。"],[779.66,787.49,98,"Form your team this week, skim the project page tonight, pick two candidate briefs, and have a working baseline by the end of week one.","这周组好队，今晚浏览一下项目页面，挑两个候选选题，第一周结束前把基线跑通。"],[787.84,794.69,98,"Next lecture, we'll turn to one of the most important application areas of LLMs, and one we touched on today.","下一讲，我们将转向大模型最重要的应用领域之一，也是今天提到过的一个。"],[795.04,799.37,98,"Medical LLMs, and the path towards generalist medical AI.","医疗大模型，以及通往通用医疗人工智能的道路。"],[799.72,802.95,98,"See you then, and good luck getting your projects started!","到时候见，祝大家项目顺利开局！"]]}]};
